1
00:00:01,582 --> 00:00:03,184
PIKACHU:
 Pika!

2
00:00:04,552 --> 00:00:09,657
( trumpets playing )

3
00:00:09,690 --> 00:00:11,325
ANNOUNCER:
 The Poké Ball,

4
00:00:11,358 --> 00:00:13,561
 an invention that's captured
the imagination

5
00:00:13,594 --> 00:00:14,796
 of people everywhere.

6
00:00:14,829 --> 00:00:16,431
 Thanks to its ability

7
00:00:16,464 --> 00:00:19,100
 to capture the most marvelous
of creatures,

8
00:00:19,133 --> 00:00:20,501
 Pokémon.

9
00:00:20,534 --> 00:00:21,602
 And to catch one

10
00:00:21,635 --> 00:00:23,471
 is an experience
like none other.

11
00:00:23,504 --> 00:00:25,506
 Each of these
spectacular species

12
00:00:25,539 --> 00:00:27,542
 has amazing powers
and attributes

13
00:00:27,575 --> 00:00:29,410
 that set them apart
from one another

14
00:00:29,443 --> 00:00:32,180
 in ways too numerous to list.

15
00:00:32,213 --> 00:00:34,182
 But unique as they are
individually,

16
00:00:34,215 --> 00:00:35,450
 together they make up

17
00:00:35,483 --> 00:00:38,453
 the incredible world
of Pokémon.

18
00:01:08,716 --> 00:01:10,351
( growling )

19
00:01:12,753 --> 00:01:16,224
Golem. Golem.

20
00:01:17,925 --> 00:01:19,460
Geodude.
Geodude.

21
00:01:19,493 --> 00:01:21,262
Geo. Geodude.

22
00:01:21,295 --> 00:01:23,631
Haunter. Haunter. Haunter.

23
00:01:25,499 --> 00:01:29,504
( growls )

24
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:35,243
Primeape.

25
00:01:44,785 --> 00:01:49,357
Wingull.

26
00:01:56,197 --> 00:01:58,199
Tentacool.

27
00:01:58,232 --> 00:02:00,168
Magikarp. Magikarp.

28
00:02:00,201 --> 00:02:01,936
Sharpedo!

29
00:02:01,969 --> 00:02:04,472
 Pokémon and people
like Ash Ketchum

30
00:02:04,505 --> 00:02:06,474
 can come together as a team.

31
00:02:06,507 --> 00:02:08,543
 For once they're captured
in a Poké Ball,

32
00:02:08,576 --> 00:02:10,845
 Pokémon bond with their human
trainers

33
00:02:10,878 --> 00:02:13,514
 as friends, partners, family.

34
00:02:13,547 --> 00:02:15,850
 On their journey of discovery,

35
00:02:15,883 --> 00:02:17,385
 trainers and their Pokémon

36
00:02:17,418 --> 00:02:20,655
 learn as much about themselves
as each other.

37
00:02:20,688 --> 00:02:22,223
 And they also realize

38
00:02:22,256 --> 00:02:23,624
 that there will always be
more Pokémon

39
00:02:23,657 --> 00:02:25,493
 than they could have
ever imagined.

40
00:02:25,526 --> 00:02:27,795
 You see, for each Pokémon
that's discovered,

41
00:02:27,828 --> 00:02:29,830
 there are dozens,
perhaps hundreds more

42
00:02:29,863 --> 00:02:31,699
 we have yet to meet.

43
00:02:31,732 --> 00:02:33,367
 One thing's for sure,

44
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:36,437
 with each of these new Pokémon
come new possibilities,

45
00:02:36,470 --> 00:02:40,542
 new stories, new friendships,
and new adventures.

46
00:02:43,377 --> 00:02:46,781
( upbeat theme playing )

47
00:03:01,662 --> 00:03:02,763
Venusaur.

48
00:03:02,797 --> 00:03:05,967
 Perhaps Pokémon trainers
aren't the only ones

49
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,902
 to seek out new species.

50
00:03:07,935 --> 00:03:10,938
 The Pokémon themselves seem
to have an innate curiosity

51
00:03:10,971 --> 00:03:14,542
 for the creatures of this world
and of worlds beyond.

52
00:03:14,575 --> 00:03:15,676
 After all,

53
00:03:15,709 --> 00:03:17,778
 we may live
on a Pokémon planet,

54
00:03:17,811 --> 00:03:21,249
 but nobody ever said
that it's the only one.

55
00:03:23,017 --> 00:03:25,353
( dramatic theme playing )

56
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:41,769
( majestic theme playing )

57
00:04:12,366 --> 00:04:15,737
( mellow theme playing )

58
00:04:35,122 --> 00:04:37,458
( indistinct chattering )

59
00:04:48,635 --> 00:04:51,939
Professor,
have you seen Tory?

60
00:04:51,972 --> 00:04:53,508
Take a look.

61
00:04:55,909 --> 00:04:57,345
YUKO:
Uh-huh.

62
00:04:57,378 --> 00:04:58,813
Impossible keeping up
with him.

63
00:05:07,054 --> 00:05:09,056
( laughing ):
Spheal.

64
00:05:09,089 --> 00:05:11,092
Wow, it's a Spheal.

65
00:05:11,125 --> 00:05:13,728
Spheal, Spheal.
Hi.

66
00:05:14,595 --> 00:05:16,831
Spheal, Spheal, Spheal.

67
00:05:16,864 --> 00:05:18,733
Spheal.

68
00:05:18,766 --> 00:05:22,703
Spheal, Spheal.
Spheal, Spheal.

69
00:05:22,736 --> 00:05:24,739
( laughs )

70
00:05:27,608 --> 00:05:29,544
Ah.

71
00:05:35,048 --> 00:05:36,784
( ominous theme playing )

72
00:05:47,895 --> 00:05:49,630
( roars )

73
00:06:00,841 --> 00:06:01,976
( panting )

74
00:06:02,009 --> 00:06:03,478
( both gasp )

75
00:06:07,114 --> 00:06:08,849
( explosion )

76
00:06:08,882 --> 00:06:10,985
( screaming )

77
00:06:15,022 --> 00:06:16,924
( creatures murmuring )

78
00:06:25,098 --> 00:06:26,734
( whimpering )

79
00:06:35,943 --> 00:06:37,445
ASH:
Tory?

80
00:06:41,782 --> 00:06:43,885
You're okay.
I've got you.

81
00:06:45,919 --> 00:06:48,456
Thank you, Daddy.

82
00:06:58,265 --> 00:07:01,202
( dramatic theme playing )

83
00:07:01,235 --> 00:07:02,703
( gasps )

84
00:07:23,891 --> 00:07:26,927
It's some kind of Pokémon,
isn't it?

85
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:28,762
Yes. Hmm.

86
00:07:28,795 --> 00:07:31,833
It's a Pokémon from outer space.

87
00:07:57,124 --> 00:07:58,893
( roars )

88
00:08:20,881 --> 00:08:23,083
Rayquaza never leaves
the ozone layer.

89
00:08:23,116 --> 00:08:24,585
Why now?

90
00:08:33,093 --> 00:08:34,695
It regenerated.

91
00:08:34,728 --> 00:08:36,797
But how's that possible?

92
00:08:45,372 --> 00:08:47,141
Let's go.
It's too dangerous.

93
00:08:47,174 --> 00:08:48,643
Yeah.

94
00:08:59,052 --> 00:09:00,855
( roaring )

95
00:09:25,846 --> 00:09:27,781
Ah!
Are you okay?

96
00:09:27,814 --> 00:09:29,149
Huh?

97
00:09:29,182 --> 00:09:30,851
( electricity crackling )

98
00:09:46,333 --> 00:09:48,869
( roars )

99
00:09:50,871 --> 00:09:53,908
Quick, follow me.
I'm right behind you.

100
00:10:13,293 --> 00:10:14,996
Whoa!

101
00:10:17,330 --> 00:10:19,100
Ah!

102
00:10:26,006 --> 00:10:27,675
( roaring )

103
00:10:32,779 --> 00:10:35,916
SPHEAL:
Spheal, Spheal, Spheal, Spheal!

104
00:10:44,424 --> 00:10:47,861
( wailing )

105
00:10:47,894 --> 00:10:50,798
MAN 1: Oh, what is it?
MAN 2: Look at that.

106
00:10:50,831 --> 00:10:53,200
( both sigh )

107
00:11:03,276 --> 00:11:05,980
( roars )

108
00:11:21,828 --> 00:11:23,964
( dramatic theme playing )

109
00:11:35,542 --> 00:11:37,912
( wailing )

110
00:12:05,872 --> 00:12:08,008
LUND:
Rayquaza is furious.

111
00:12:09,242 --> 00:12:12,079
Another Pokémon crossing
into its territory

112
00:12:12,112 --> 00:12:14,081
has obviously threatened it.

113
00:12:37,504 --> 00:12:39,840
Huh?

114
00:12:45,078 --> 00:12:46,814
LUND:
Fire the laser.

115
00:12:59,559 --> 00:13:02,229
Raise our trajectory
by 0.5.

116
00:13:02,262 --> 00:13:04,098
Right.

117
00:13:10,237 --> 00:13:13,307
That's the frequency.
Finally, in sync.

118
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:14,575
That means...?
Yes.

119
00:13:14,608 --> 00:13:19,113
The crystal should regenerate
if we keep the laser on target.

120
00:13:21,181 --> 00:13:24,351
We will succeed.
We have to.

121
00:13:43,937 --> 00:13:45,973
( alarm beeping )

122
00:13:49,576 --> 00:13:51,879
We overloaded the regulator.

123
00:13:59,953 --> 00:14:01,355
YUKO:
It was just one small component

124
00:14:01,388 --> 00:14:02,522
that malfunctioned.

125
00:14:02,555 --> 00:14:04,091
A simple replacement.

126
00:14:04,124 --> 00:14:05,659
LUND:
Good. We'll try again

127
00:14:05,692 --> 00:14:07,027
after it's fixed.

128
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:08,362
YUKO:
Yes, sir.

129
00:14:08,395 --> 00:14:09,496
Huh?

130
00:14:09,529 --> 00:14:10,998
( laughs )

131
00:14:12,165 --> 00:14:14,101
Guess what?
I'm gonna tell you

132
00:14:14,134 --> 00:14:15,402
all about this book
I'm reading.

133
00:14:15,435 --> 00:14:16,637
It's so good.

134
00:14:16,670 --> 00:14:18,005
MAN 1:
Once that part's replaced,

135
00:14:18,038 --> 00:14:19,172
we're almost home.

136
00:14:19,205 --> 00:14:21,408
MAN 2:
Yeah, we're so close.

137
00:14:27,681 --> 00:14:30,951
I was right.
I did see it glow.

138
00:14:35,088 --> 00:14:37,424
( dramatic theme playing )

139
00:15:12,459 --> 00:15:14,728
BOTH:
Wow!

140
00:15:14,761 --> 00:15:17,097
WINGULL:
Wingull, Wingull, Wingull,

141
00:15:17,130 --> 00:15:21,201
Wingull, Wingull,
Wingull!

142
00:15:21,234 --> 00:15:24,037
PELIPPER:
Pelipper.

143
00:15:24,070 --> 00:15:26,340
 On his journey
to become a Pokémon master,

144
00:15:26,373 --> 00:15:29,242
 Ash Ketchum and his friends
arrive in Larousse City,

145
00:15:29,275 --> 00:15:32,512
 the headquarters for anything
and everything high-tech.

146
00:15:32,545 --> 00:15:35,282
 But he's not here
for the gadgets and gizmos.

147
00:15:35,315 --> 00:15:37,317
 Ash is itching for action

148
00:15:37,350 --> 00:15:40,087
 at the town's
famous Battle Tower.

149
00:15:41,087 --> 00:15:43,223
Pelipper.
Pelipper.

150
00:15:44,591 --> 00:15:46,160
Huh?

151
00:15:47,494 --> 00:15:49,330
( whimpering )

152
00:15:52,732 --> 00:15:54,501
( all panting )

153
00:15:57,370 --> 00:15:59,106
( panting )

154
00:16:02,642 --> 00:16:04,445
( squeals )

155
00:16:07,380 --> 00:16:09,316
( chattering )

156
00:16:21,694 --> 00:16:24,431
( both laughing )

157
00:16:24,464 --> 00:16:26,133
Yay!

158
00:16:31,805 --> 00:16:35,142
Munch. Munch.
Munch.

159
00:16:37,744 --> 00:16:39,380
( laughs )

160
00:16:48,621 --> 00:16:50,324
Munch.

161
00:16:53,827 --> 00:16:56,196
Munch.

162
00:16:57,664 --> 00:16:59,166
Munch.

163
00:17:04,337 --> 00:17:05,439
Munch.

164
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:09,343
Munch.

165
00:17:10,777 --> 00:17:12,579
Munch.

166
00:17:25,859 --> 00:17:29,463
Munch. Munch.

167
00:17:38,872 --> 00:17:40,307
 Welcome.

168
00:17:40,340 --> 00:17:41,875
 You are now
in Larousse City.

169
00:17:41,908 --> 00:17:43,243
 Welcome again.

170
00:17:43,276 --> 00:17:45,112
Cool.
It's so cute.

171
00:17:45,145 --> 00:17:46,313
A robot.

172
00:17:46,346 --> 00:17:48,849
What could be better than that?
Pika.

173
00:17:48,882 --> 00:17:50,851
Being greeted by a real live
beautiful girl

174
00:17:50,884 --> 00:17:52,352
could be one thing.

175
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:55,489
 Smile.

176
00:18:03,696 --> 00:18:05,699
 Visitor data confirmed.

177
00:18:05,732 --> 00:18:08,568
 Citizenship and point of origin
recorded.

178
00:18:08,601 --> 00:18:11,605
 These will serve
as your passports.

179
00:18:12,705 --> 00:18:13,840
Our passports?

180
00:18:13,873 --> 00:18:15,308
 While in Larousse City,

181
00:18:15,341 --> 00:18:16,877
 keep them with you
at all times.

182
00:18:16,910 --> 00:18:21,248
 Your passports can be used
for shopping and other needs.

183
00:18:24,817 --> 00:18:27,621
Don't think I'll be sending
this one home.

184
00:18:27,654 --> 00:18:30,624
So I wonder which way to go
for the Battle Tower.

185
00:18:30,657 --> 00:18:32,126
Pika.

186
00:18:33,259 --> 00:18:35,629
Help!
Pika!

187
00:18:37,664 --> 00:18:40,500
Hey, Ash,
quit messing around.

188
00:18:40,533 --> 00:18:42,469
A moving sidewalk.

189
00:18:46,206 --> 00:18:47,908
SID:
Dude, you're swimming upstream.

190
00:18:47,941 --> 00:18:50,377
There is an easier way.

191
00:18:50,410 --> 00:18:52,479
Well, if I ever get off
of this thing,

192
00:18:52,512 --> 00:18:53,880
then maybe you could show it
to me!

193
00:18:53,913 --> 00:18:55,615
Pika!

194
00:18:55,648 --> 00:18:56,883
Nice fall.

195
00:18:56,916 --> 00:18:58,619
Nice fall.

196
00:19:01,688 --> 00:19:02,856
Blaze.

197
00:19:02,889 --> 00:19:05,959
Help him out, Blaziken, okay?

198
00:19:05,992 --> 00:19:08,262
Blaze.

199
00:19:11,631 --> 00:19:14,535
Blaze. Blaze.

200
00:19:15,868 --> 00:19:17,804
Hey, thanks a lot.
Pikachu.

201
00:19:17,837 --> 00:19:19,539
Sure, no need to thank me.

202
00:19:19,572 --> 00:19:22,742
I just couldn't continue
watching you look like a fool.

203
00:19:22,775 --> 00:19:24,511
What?

204
00:19:24,544 --> 00:19:26,846
SID:
So I guess you're all new
in town, huh?

205
00:19:26,879 --> 00:19:29,349
RAFE:
Well, if you're heading
for the Battle Tower,

206
00:19:29,382 --> 00:19:30,784
you should try
going this way.

207
00:19:30,817 --> 00:19:34,254
AUDREY: Be careful.
KATHRYN: Don't fall.

208
00:19:34,287 --> 00:19:36,489
My name's Ash
from Pallet Town.

209
00:19:36,522 --> 00:19:38,225
How'd you like to battle
with me?

210
00:19:38,258 --> 00:19:40,827
Watch out,
my brother Rafe's really strong.

211
00:19:40,860 --> 00:19:43,296
Blaziken too.
Blaze.

212
00:19:43,329 --> 00:19:45,565
Yeah, I'd love to have
a battle with you, Ash.

213
00:19:45,598 --> 00:19:47,667
Let's get together
at the Battle Tower, okay?

214
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:50,971
So we're finally gonna
settle this today, right, Rafe?

215
00:19:51,004 --> 00:19:53,306
Hello, my bespectacled beauty.

216
00:19:53,339 --> 00:19:55,242
I'm Brock.
Stop!

217
00:19:56,276 --> 00:19:58,011
Well, I guess you could say
that your friend here

218
00:19:58,044 --> 00:19:59,879
has really fallen
for Rebecca, huh?

219
00:19:59,912 --> 00:20:01,548
She's a good Metagross trainer,

220
00:20:01,581 --> 00:20:03,350
likes to use her laptop
for strategy.

221
00:20:03,383 --> 00:20:06,820
So my name is Sid.
Blastoise is my partner.

222
00:20:06,853 --> 00:20:08,321
Hi, I'm May.

223
00:20:08,354 --> 00:20:11,358
And this is my brother, Max.

224
00:20:11,391 --> 00:20:14,228
Hey, you're kind of cute.
Kind of?

225
00:20:15,528 --> 00:20:17,397
And kind of crazy too.

226
00:20:17,430 --> 00:20:19,666
Look, the Battle Tower.

227
00:20:21,367 --> 00:20:23,637
Look, Pikachu,
it's right there.

228
00:20:24,637 --> 00:20:27,541
I can't wait.
Pika.

229
00:20:31,344 --> 00:20:34,014
ASH:
I'll be back as soon
as I'm registered.

230
00:20:34,047 --> 00:20:36,416
MAX:
Okay, then we'll head
to the stands.

231
00:20:36,449 --> 00:20:37,718
ASH:
See you.

232
00:20:38,885 --> 00:20:40,554
There, let's hurry.

233
00:20:41,688 --> 00:20:42,789
( computer beeps )

234
00:20:44,023 --> 00:20:45,358
Ah.

235
00:20:45,391 --> 00:20:46,760
( laughs )

236
00:20:48,995 --> 00:20:51,665
Hmm. Uh-oh.

237
00:20:51,698 --> 00:20:53,267
Now where are we?

238
00:20:56,469 --> 00:20:59,473
Oh, wow, there's a library too.
Pika.

239
00:21:06,079 --> 00:21:08,548
Excuse me.
Pika!

240
00:21:09,849 --> 00:21:12,752
Hold on,
what do you running away for?

241
00:21:12,785 --> 00:21:13,920
Pika.

242
00:21:13,953 --> 00:21:16,556
Wait! Hold up!

243
00:21:19,926 --> 00:21:21,594
Hi. Let me start that again.

244
00:21:21,627 --> 00:21:22,862
We're on our way to a battle

245
00:21:22,895 --> 00:21:24,531
but we don't know
how to get there.

246
00:21:24,564 --> 00:21:27,701
So we're kind of lost.
Pika, Pika.

247
00:21:30,636 --> 00:21:33,373
Wait, we just wanna-- Hi.

248
00:21:33,406 --> 00:21:35,008
Are you ready for your battle?

249
00:21:35,041 --> 00:21:37,644
Right this way, gentlemen.

250
00:21:37,677 --> 00:21:39,412
But you don't understand.

251
00:21:39,445 --> 00:21:41,681
If you hurry up,
you two might just make it.

252
00:21:41,714 --> 00:21:43,583
But I haven't registered yet.

253
00:21:43,616 --> 00:21:45,919
That will all happen
automatically.

254
00:21:45,952 --> 00:21:47,688
Now, good luck, you two.

255
00:21:51,457 --> 00:21:52,959
COMPUTER:
 Passports confirmed.

256
00:21:52,992 --> 00:21:55,995
 Two youth-level participants
entered successfully.

257
00:21:56,028 --> 00:21:58,899
Great, and just in time.
Pika.

258
00:22:00,867 --> 00:22:04,437
 Entry for participants
in the first round is closed.

259
00:22:04,470 --> 00:22:06,106
 Please try again next time.

260
00:22:06,139 --> 00:22:07,607
What?

261
00:22:08,741 --> 00:22:11,611
 Now introducing
our first entry.

262
00:22:15,114 --> 00:22:16,750
Pika.

263
00:22:19,886 --> 00:22:22,756
Here we go.
Pikachu.

264
00:22:26,692 --> 00:22:29,028
ANNOUNCER:
 Our first match will be
an official

265
00:22:29,061 --> 00:22:30,697
 Battle Tower tag team event.

266
00:22:30,730 --> 00:22:32,999
 Remember to cheer
for your favorites.

267
00:22:33,032 --> 00:22:35,435
Tag team, huh? Yeah.

268
00:22:35,468 --> 00:22:37,704
 We have Ash Ketchum
in the blue corner,

269
00:22:37,737 --> 00:22:39,939
 a trainer all the way
from Pallet Town.

270
00:22:39,972 --> 00:22:43,076
 And his tag partner Tory,
a local trainer.

271
00:22:43,109 --> 00:22:44,778
All right, Tory, good luck.

272
00:22:44,811 --> 00:22:48,148
I wonder how Ash
got entered so quickly.

273
00:22:48,181 --> 00:22:50,016
By cutting in front of me.

274
00:22:50,049 --> 00:22:51,618
Rebecca,

275
00:22:51,651 --> 00:22:53,052
there comes a time
in a man's life

276
00:22:53,085 --> 00:22:55,755
when he's presented with
the gift of love at first sight.

277
00:22:55,788 --> 00:22:59,693
How about pain at first pull?
Not the ear.

278
00:23:01,227 --> 00:23:05,165
Professor Lund,
take a look at this.

279
00:23:05,198 --> 00:23:07,834
Tory?
In a Pokémon battle?

280
00:23:09,168 --> 00:23:10,670
 And in the red corner,

281
00:23:10,703 --> 00:23:12,906
 we have two trainers
from South City,

282
00:23:12,939 --> 00:23:14,607
 Rafe and Sid.

283
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:17,477
Hey, Ash,
you sure didn't waste any time.

284
00:23:19,645 --> 00:23:21,881
Of course not,
I couldn't wait to beat you.

285
00:23:21,914 --> 00:23:23,550
Hey! May!

286
00:23:23,583 --> 00:23:24,918
Make sure you watch.

287
00:23:24,951 --> 00:23:27,487
I'm dedicating this battle
to you.

288
00:23:29,956 --> 00:23:32,926
 The basic rule in all tag team
battles is teamwork.

289
00:23:32,959 --> 00:23:35,228
 Each trainer uses a single
Pokémon

290
00:23:35,261 --> 00:23:36,796
 and works with his teammate.

291
00:23:36,829 --> 00:23:40,900
 And now, trainers,
bring out your Pokémon.

292
00:23:40,933 --> 00:23:43,737
All right. Here goes.
Here goes.

293
00:23:46,272 --> 00:23:48,942
Blaze.
Blastoise.

294
00:23:48,975 --> 00:23:50,977
Pikachu, I choose you.

295
00:23:51,010 --> 00:23:53,012
Pika. Pikachu.

296
00:23:53,045 --> 00:23:55,515
Tory, what Pokémon
are you gonna use?

297
00:23:55,548 --> 00:23:57,550
No, Ash,
I don't have any Pokémon.

298
00:23:57,583 --> 00:23:58,785
But...
Pika.

299
00:23:58,818 --> 00:24:00,687
 There seems to be a problem.

300
00:24:00,720 --> 00:24:02,689
 We've seen only one Pokémon
from the blue corner.

301
00:24:02,722 --> 00:24:04,858
See, I was trying
to tell you.

302
00:24:04,891 --> 00:24:07,560
I'm not a trainer.
I can't battle.

303
00:24:07,593 --> 00:24:08,795
But this could end up

304
00:24:08,828 --> 00:24:10,797
being my only chance
to battle Rafe.

305
00:24:10,830 --> 00:24:13,867
Hey, I know what,
I'll loan you one of my Pokémon.

306
00:24:13,900 --> 00:24:14,901
What do you say?

307
00:24:14,934 --> 00:24:16,870
Come on, that'll work.
But...

308
00:24:18,170 --> 00:24:20,106
 Will the blue corner forfeit?

309
00:24:20,139 --> 00:24:22,675
Don't let me down, Tory.

310
00:24:22,708 --> 00:24:25,011
Well, if I have to.

311
00:24:27,146 --> 00:24:29,949
Torkoal.

312
00:24:29,982 --> 00:24:32,719
 So looks like
we have our Pokémon.

313
00:24:32,752 --> 00:24:35,088
 Ready for a battle,
because here we go!

314
00:24:35,121 --> 00:24:38,258
Let's do it.
Blaziken, use Blaze Kick now.

315
00:24:38,291 --> 00:24:42,161
Blaziken.

316
00:24:42,194 --> 00:24:44,130
Dodge, Pikachu.

317
00:24:44,163 --> 00:24:45,765
Pika.

318
00:24:47,166 --> 00:24:48,801
Go, Blastoise, Hydro Pump.

319
00:24:48,834 --> 00:24:51,771
Blastoise.
Pika!

320
00:24:51,804 --> 00:24:54,741
 It's a dazzling combination
from the red corner.

321
00:24:54,774 --> 00:24:57,811
Blastoise, Bubble Attack.
Blastoise.

322
00:24:59,979 --> 00:25:03,650
Torkoal. Tory, you have to tell
Torkoal to do something.

323
00:25:03,683 --> 00:25:05,585
But I don't know
what to tell it.

324
00:25:05,618 --> 00:25:09,155
Blastoise, Rapid Spin.
Blastoise.

325
00:25:09,188 --> 00:25:12,058
Blastoise!

326
00:25:14,860 --> 00:25:17,731
Torkoal!

327
00:25:18,831 --> 00:25:21,034
Blast.

328
00:25:22,168 --> 00:25:23,737
( breathing heavily )

329
00:25:32,244 --> 00:25:34,014
Blastoise.

330
00:25:35,214 --> 00:25:37,350
Blastoise.

331
00:25:37,383 --> 00:25:40,887
Pikachu, use Thunderbolt.
Cover Torkoal.

332
00:25:40,920 --> 00:25:42,889
Pikachu!

333
00:25:42,922 --> 00:25:47,360
Blastoise.
Blaziken.

334
00:25:47,393 --> 00:25:49,329
Blastoise, Skull Bash, go.

335
00:25:49,362 --> 00:25:50,930
Blastoise.

336
00:25:50,963 --> 00:25:53,066
Torkoal.

337
00:25:53,099 --> 00:25:55,001
Torkoal.
 Looks like the blue corner

338
00:25:55,034 --> 00:25:57,804
 just can't seem to get it
together as a team.

339
00:25:57,837 --> 00:26:00,006
Man, Ash's partner
isn't doing anything

340
00:26:00,039 --> 00:26:01,007
to help him out at all.

341
00:26:01,040 --> 00:26:03,343
I don't see how he could win.

342
00:26:03,376 --> 00:26:05,812
Come on, do something.

343
00:26:07,079 --> 00:26:09,215
Tory, don't worry,
I'll take care of it.

344
00:26:09,248 --> 00:26:11,117
Flamethrower, Torkoal, go.

345
00:26:11,150 --> 00:26:12,285
Torkoal.
Pika.

346
00:26:12,318 --> 00:26:15,121
Torkoal!

347
00:26:15,154 --> 00:26:17,757
 Oh, a Flamethrower
from Torkoal,

348
00:26:17,790 --> 00:26:19,225
 but it hit Pikachu.

349
00:26:19,258 --> 00:26:22,028
Torkoal, Torkoal.

350
00:26:22,061 --> 00:26:22,895
How embarrassing.

351
00:26:22,929 --> 00:26:25,832
So, Rafe,
wanna finish this one up?

352
00:26:25,865 --> 00:26:28,668
Let's go. Blaziken, Overheat.

353
00:26:28,701 --> 00:26:30,737
Blaziken!

354
00:26:30,770 --> 00:26:35,241
Pika! Pika!

355
00:26:35,274 --> 00:26:37,010
Pikachu, Torkoal.

356
00:26:37,043 --> 00:26:38,711
 And that's it.

357
00:26:38,744 --> 00:26:40,913
 Pikachu and Torkoal
are unable to battle.

358
00:26:40,946 --> 00:26:45,652
 Rafe and Sid are the winners.
Congratulations.

359
00:26:47,153 --> 00:26:50,189
Blaze.
Blastoise.

360
00:26:50,222 --> 00:26:52,258
( laughs )

361
00:26:52,291 --> 00:26:53,994
( elevator dings )

362
00:26:58,431 --> 00:27:00,900
Tory.
Daddy.

363
00:27:00,933 --> 00:27:02,802
We just watched
your Pokémon battle.

364
00:27:02,835 --> 00:27:04,070
I'm incredibly proud.

365
00:27:04,103 --> 00:27:06,673
Don't be.
It was all an accident,

366
00:27:06,706 --> 00:27:09,042
wasn't even supposed to happen.

367
00:27:11,043 --> 00:27:12,178
ALL:
Huh?

368
00:27:17,416 --> 00:27:20,820
Yuko, meeting you reminds me
of a time in my life

369
00:27:20,853 --> 00:27:22,455
when I too spent long hours

370
00:27:22,488 --> 00:27:24,157
toiling as a professor's
assistant.

371
00:27:24,190 --> 00:27:26,392
I'm sure Professor Ivy
would be happy

372
00:27:26,425 --> 00:27:28,161
to vouch for my work.

373
00:27:28,194 --> 00:27:31,197
And I'll be happy to vouch
for his insanity.

374
00:27:32,765 --> 00:27:35,201
We apologize for the mix-up
with your battle.

375
00:27:35,234 --> 00:27:36,402
The truth is,

376
00:27:36,435 --> 00:27:38,905
Tory is completely afraid
of Pokémon.

377
00:27:38,938 --> 00:27:40,973
How could he be afraid
of Pokémon?

378
00:27:41,006 --> 00:27:43,409
Well, about four years ago,

379
00:27:43,442 --> 00:27:45,778
he had a very traumatic
experience

380
00:27:45,811 --> 00:27:48,081
and it left him terrified
of them.

381
00:27:48,114 --> 00:27:52,218
Sadly, he still hasn't managed
to get over those fears.

382
00:28:23,516 --> 00:28:26,185
Wow, I shouldn't have pushed him
so hard.

383
00:28:26,218 --> 00:28:29,155
But underneath it all,
I think he loves them.

384
00:28:29,188 --> 00:28:31,224
All he really needs
is the chance

385
00:28:31,257 --> 00:28:33,226
to get to know them,
that's all.

386
00:28:33,259 --> 00:28:35,495
I'm sure that's all it'll take.

387
00:28:35,528 --> 00:28:38,831
Fine. Then I'll give him
that chance.

388
00:28:38,864 --> 00:28:40,800
All he needs now
is to become friends

389
00:28:40,833 --> 00:28:41,968
with me and Pikachu.

390
00:28:42,001 --> 00:28:44,937
Right, pal?
Pika.

391
00:28:44,970 --> 00:28:46,939
I wanna help too.
So do I.

392
00:28:46,972 --> 00:28:48,341
Me too.
Cool.

393
00:28:48,374 --> 00:28:50,910
So, what do you say we all go
and look for Tory, okay?

394
00:28:50,943 --> 00:28:52,078
ALL:
Yeah!

395
00:28:52,111 --> 00:28:54,847
You're awful kind.
Thank you.

396
00:28:54,880 --> 00:28:56,883
( whimpering )

397
00:28:58,384 --> 00:28:59,919
( grunts )

398
00:29:06,125 --> 00:29:09,062
ASH: Tory?
PIKACHU: Pika?

399
00:29:13,933 --> 00:29:15,802
( both chattering )

400
00:29:17,570 --> 00:29:19,105
( both squeal )

401
00:29:21,106 --> 00:29:22,308
( laughs )

402
00:29:28,180 --> 00:29:29,348
Later.

403
00:29:29,381 --> 00:29:31,785
Pika.

404
00:29:33,352 --> 00:29:35,321
( both chattering )

405
00:29:40,860 --> 00:29:44,998
Munch. Munch.

406
00:29:52,338 --> 00:29:54,874
Munch. Munch.

407
00:30:00,246 --> 00:30:01,881
Munch.

408
00:30:07,386 --> 00:30:09,088
Munch.

409
00:30:22,501 --> 00:30:25,004
TORY:
Hey, come on out.

410
00:30:25,037 --> 00:30:26,205
Where are you?

411
00:30:26,238 --> 00:30:29,108
I wanna tell you
something important.

412
00:30:35,514 --> 00:30:37,016
( laughs )

413
00:30:43,255 --> 00:30:45,024
You'll never guess
what I just did.

414
00:30:45,057 --> 00:30:46,559
I helped out a Pokémon.

415
00:30:46,592 --> 00:30:48,895
Because it had its head stuck
inside a garbage can

416
00:30:48,928 --> 00:30:50,496
and so I helped to get it out.

417
00:30:50,529 --> 00:30:52,231
Isn't that cool?

418
00:30:52,264 --> 00:30:54,434
( laughing )

419
00:30:58,637 --> 00:31:01,207
( dramatic theme playing )

420
00:31:28,033 --> 00:31:30,169
( both panting )

421
00:31:35,341 --> 00:31:37,076
( all gasp )

422
00:31:41,146 --> 00:31:44,350
Hey, what are those lights?

423
00:31:44,383 --> 00:31:47,253
And I was even part
of a Pokémon battle too.

424
00:31:47,286 --> 00:31:50,556
Of course, I wasn't very good,
so that part kind of stunk.

425
00:31:50,589 --> 00:31:53,693
ASH:
Hey, who are you talking to?

426
00:31:53,726 --> 00:31:55,295
Pika.

427
00:32:06,472 --> 00:32:09,075
Hey, it's gone.

428
00:32:11,076 --> 00:32:14,347
Come on, who was it?
None of your business.

429
00:32:14,380 --> 00:32:15,681
Why, would it hurt
to tell me?

430
00:32:15,714 --> 00:32:19,118
Stop.
Leave me alone, okay?

431
00:32:19,151 --> 00:32:20,586
( grunting )
Wait a minute.

432
00:32:20,619 --> 00:32:22,455
If this town
is so high-tech,

433
00:32:22,488 --> 00:32:24,423
why don't they
have moving sidewalks?

434
00:32:24,456 --> 00:32:26,726
Or robots
that serve hamburgers?

435
00:32:26,759 --> 00:32:28,561
Yeah, keep dreaming.

436
00:32:28,594 --> 00:32:32,365
( all groaning )

437
00:32:32,398 --> 00:32:34,333
BOY:
I'll take a hamburger, please.

438
00:32:34,366 --> 00:32:36,302
 Hamburger.

439
00:32:41,240 --> 00:32:42,508
Yum.

440
00:32:43,642 --> 00:32:45,311
( all laugh )

441
00:32:45,344 --> 00:32:47,279
ALL:
Hamburgers, please.

442
00:32:47,312 --> 00:32:49,582
 Passport. Passport.
Passport.

443
00:32:49,615 --> 00:32:51,083
What's a passport?

444
00:32:51,116 --> 00:32:52,718
Well, I have no idea
what kind of pass

445
00:32:52,751 --> 00:32:54,186
he's talking about.

446
00:32:54,219 --> 00:32:56,522
But, Meowth,
please stop calling me sport.

447
00:32:56,555 --> 00:32:58,524
You idiot. Hamburger!

448
00:32:58,557 --> 00:33:02,161
Hey, that ain't right.
Cheeseburger!

449
00:33:02,194 --> 00:33:04,330
 Alert. Alert. Alert.
Now, now, now!

450
00:33:07,533 --> 00:33:09,502
( Meowth grunting )
JESSIE: Come on! Come on!

451
00:33:09,535 --> 00:33:12,071
 Come on, come on.
( Jessie screaming )

452
00:33:12,104 --> 00:33:14,473
That was rude.
Maybe she takes our order?

453
00:33:14,506 --> 00:33:18,244
Yeah? Well, I'm pretty good
at giving orders.

454
00:33:18,277 --> 00:33:21,447
So I'm gonna have
five hamburgers well-done

455
00:33:21,480 --> 00:33:23,449
and don't forget
the french fries.

456
00:33:23,482 --> 00:33:24,784
 Well done, it is.

457
00:33:24,817 --> 00:33:27,253
( screaming )

458
00:33:27,286 --> 00:33:28,821
Jessie got fried!

459
00:33:28,854 --> 00:33:31,090
Without the burgers.

460
00:33:31,123 --> 00:33:34,160
I think we should battle
together again.

461
00:33:34,193 --> 00:33:36,095
Bet we'll get it right
next time.

462
00:33:36,128 --> 00:33:38,697
Why do you keep following me?

463
00:33:38,730 --> 00:33:40,533
WINGULL:
Gull. Gull. Wingull.

464
00:33:40,566 --> 00:33:42,135
Ah!

465
00:33:43,335 --> 00:33:46,105
Are you okay?
Pikachu?

466
00:33:46,138 --> 00:33:48,207
Ah!
Pika.

467
00:33:49,408 --> 00:33:51,143
Gee, thanks.

468
00:33:51,176 --> 00:33:52,845
Why'd you have to go
and push me?

469
00:33:52,878 --> 00:33:56,082
MAY:
Ash, stop.

470
00:33:56,115 --> 00:33:58,584
Don't start something.
Okay.

471
00:34:00,586 --> 00:34:02,621
Oh! Oh!

472
00:34:02,654 --> 00:34:04,723
Hey, I know.

473
00:34:04,756 --> 00:34:06,358
Pika.

474
00:34:06,391 --> 00:34:08,494
( upbeat theme playing )

475
00:34:13,699 --> 00:34:16,435
Hmm. Perfect. Dig in.

476
00:34:16,468 --> 00:34:17,770
I'll go first.

477
00:34:17,803 --> 00:34:20,806
Second.
Hold on.

478
00:34:20,839 --> 00:34:23,342
Whoa, it's hot.

479
00:34:23,375 --> 00:34:24,343
Yum.

480
00:34:24,376 --> 00:34:26,779
There's nothing that can stop
an argument

481
00:34:26,812 --> 00:34:28,581
better than a bunch
of full mouths.

482
00:34:28,614 --> 00:34:32,085
Try some, Tory,
it's really good.

483
00:34:39,758 --> 00:34:41,694
You're right.
Told you so.

484
00:34:41,727 --> 00:34:43,662
( all laughing )

485
00:34:43,695 --> 00:34:46,232
ASH:
Guys, look at
all those Pokémon.

486
00:34:46,265 --> 00:34:47,633
SEEDOT:
Seedot.

487
00:34:47,666 --> 00:34:49,268
Well, hi.

488
00:34:49,301 --> 00:34:52,338
There's plenty of Pokémon food
so don't be shy.

489
00:34:52,371 --> 00:34:54,640
There. Dig in, guys.
Seedot.

490
00:34:54,673 --> 00:34:57,443
Seedot. Seedot. Seedot.

491
00:34:57,476 --> 00:35:00,679
Tory, don't you think
they're the cutest?

492
00:35:00,712 --> 00:35:02,248
Yeah.
Hey,

493
00:35:02,281 --> 00:35:03,749
I bet they'd
let you pet them.

494
00:35:03,782 --> 00:35:05,384
Pika.
( gasps )

495
00:35:05,417 --> 00:35:07,120
Pika.

496
00:35:09,788 --> 00:35:11,357
( grunts )

497
00:35:11,390 --> 00:35:12,658
( gasping )
Pika?

498
00:35:15,460 --> 00:35:18,264
Thanks, guys. I'm sorry.

499
00:35:19,198 --> 00:35:21,500
Well, we tried.
Pika.

500
00:35:21,533 --> 00:35:24,303
I'm sure we'll get through
to him eventually.

501
00:35:24,336 --> 00:35:25,905
Seedot. Seedot.
Oh, guys!

502
00:35:25,938 --> 00:35:27,406
Munch. Munch. Munch.

503
00:35:28,574 --> 00:35:29,609
( all gasp )

504
00:35:29,642 --> 00:35:32,378
Oh, no, it's a Munchlax,
and they love to eat.

505
00:35:32,411 --> 00:35:35,447
Well, guess
it's doing what it loves.

506
00:35:35,480 --> 00:35:38,551
Hey, you,
that was our lunch.

507
00:35:43,589 --> 00:35:44,690
Munch!

508
00:35:45,958 --> 00:35:48,794
Munch. Munch. Munch.

509
00:35:48,827 --> 00:35:50,296
Munch.

510
00:35:51,230 --> 00:35:52,531
ALL:
Wow.

511
00:35:52,564 --> 00:35:55,267
Hey, it's a Plusle
and Minun.

512
00:35:55,300 --> 00:35:56,602
Hi, cuties.

513
00:35:56,635 --> 00:35:58,370
Pika. Pika.

514
00:35:58,403 --> 00:36:01,574
( both chattering )

515
00:36:01,607 --> 00:36:03,542
Pika. Pika.

516
00:36:03,575 --> 00:36:06,479
PELIPPERS:
Pelipper. Pelipper.

517
00:36:11,416 --> 00:36:13,919
MURKROWS:
Murkrow. Murkrow. Murkrow.

518
00:36:13,952 --> 00:36:16,489
( suspenseful theme playing )

519
00:36:17,990 --> 00:36:20,626
Murkrow. Murkrow. Murkrow.

520
00:36:23,528 --> 00:36:27,466
( explosion )
( Murkrows shouting )

521
00:36:43,482 --> 00:36:45,351
( dramatic theme playing )

522
00:37:10,442 --> 00:37:12,511
MAX:
There's that light
in the sky again.

523
00:37:12,544 --> 00:37:13,545
Awesome.

524
00:37:13,578 --> 00:37:15,614
Pika.
It's beautiful.

525
00:37:15,647 --> 00:37:18,384
Well, but that's impossible.

526
00:37:18,417 --> 00:37:21,353
What is?
That's called an aurora,

527
00:37:21,386 --> 00:37:22,588
but it can only be seen

528
00:37:22,621 --> 00:37:24,757
at the north
and the south poles.

529
00:37:24,790 --> 00:37:26,425
Strange.

530
00:37:26,458 --> 00:37:27,826
Well, then I guess,

531
00:37:27,859 --> 00:37:30,062
we're lucky to be able
to see it here, right?

532
00:37:30,095 --> 00:37:31,563
The same kind of luck

533
00:37:31,596 --> 00:37:34,500
that brought you
and me together, right, babe?

534
00:37:34,533 --> 00:37:36,869
Not sure what kind of luck
that was.

535
00:37:36,902 --> 00:37:38,337
Hi, beautiful.

536
00:37:38,370 --> 00:37:40,773
If you're looking
for a real phenomenon,

537
00:37:40,806 --> 00:37:44,076
stop looking in your computer
and spend some time with me.

538
00:37:44,109 --> 00:37:49,782
Okay, you leaving her alone,
that's a phenomenon.

539
00:37:49,815 --> 00:37:52,651
Well, look who's still in town.
So?

540
00:37:52,684 --> 00:37:54,553
Well, after
that devastating defeat

541
00:37:54,586 --> 00:37:55,854
in front
of thousands of people,

542
00:37:55,887 --> 00:37:57,656
I thought you might be
a little embarrassed

543
00:37:57,689 --> 00:37:59,558
to show your face.
Oh, yeah?

544
00:37:59,591 --> 00:38:02,661
How about a rematch tomorrow
in the Battle Tower?

545
00:38:02,694 --> 00:38:03,495
No problem.

546
00:38:03,528 --> 00:38:06,732
I'll beat you anytime
and anywhere.

547
00:38:06,765 --> 00:38:09,769
I wouldn't count on that.
Pika.

548
00:38:11,136 --> 00:38:14,707
Hey, I know you.
Tory.

549
00:38:16,541 --> 00:38:21,347
Hey, you guys.
Yuko and I made these for you.

550
00:38:21,380 --> 00:38:23,115
MAX:
Cool. Pokémon cookies.

551
00:38:23,148 --> 00:38:24,717
KATHRYN: Cute.
AUDREY: Yummy.

552
00:38:24,750 --> 00:38:26,618
ASH:
Come on out, everyone.

553
00:38:26,651 --> 00:38:28,787
( Bree Sharp's "The Side
of Paradise" playing )

554
00:38:28,820 --> 00:38:31,357
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

555
00:38:31,390 --> 00:38:32,958
 ♪ La, la, la, la
La, la, la ♪

556
00:38:32,991 --> 00:38:36,028
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

557
00:38:36,061 --> 00:38:37,563
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la, la ♪

558
00:38:38,730 --> 00:38:40,032
( grunting )

559
00:38:40,065 --> 00:38:42,034
 ♪ There's a place I know ♪

560
00:38:42,067 --> 00:38:44,036
 ♪ It's always jumping ♪

561
00:38:44,069 --> 00:38:45,437
 ♪ I'm thinking
We should go ♪

562
00:38:45,470 --> 00:38:48,607
 ♪ And leave our worries ♪

563
00:38:48,640 --> 00:38:50,409
 ♪ You got a friend in me ♪

564
00:38:50,442 --> 00:38:52,578
 ♪ And I'll tell you
Something ♪

565
00:38:52,611 --> 00:38:56,648
 ♪ This time
Could be extraordinary ♪

566
00:38:56,681 --> 00:39:00,853
 ♪ When shadows fall
You're feeling small ♪

567
00:39:00,886 --> 00:39:05,124
 ♪ It looks like walls
Are closing in ♪

568
00:39:05,157 --> 00:39:06,458
 ♪ Don't be afraid ♪

569
00:39:06,491 --> 00:39:08,093
 ♪ The dark will fade ♪

570
00:39:08,126 --> 00:39:10,095
 ♪ Just take my hand ♪

571
00:39:10,128 --> 00:39:12,431
 ♪ And look again ♪

572
00:39:12,464 --> 00:39:14,733
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

573
00:39:14,766 --> 00:39:16,468
 ♪ Is where I want to be ♪

574
00:39:16,501 --> 00:39:18,937
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

575
00:39:18,970 --> 00:39:20,639
 ♪ For you and me ♪

576
00:39:20,672 --> 00:39:22,841
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

577
00:39:22,874 --> 00:39:24,777
 ♪ What you get
Is what you see ♪

578
00:39:24,810 --> 00:39:28,947
 ♪ And I never thought
I'd see a place as nice ♪

579
00:39:28,980 --> 00:39:30,616
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

580
00:39:30,649 --> 00:39:32,151
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

581
00:39:32,184 --> 00:39:34,052
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la, la ♪

582
00:39:34,085 --> 00:39:36,588
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

583
00:39:36,621 --> 00:39:38,757
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

584
00:39:38,790 --> 00:39:43,028
 ♪ Forget about the pain
And doubt ♪

585
00:39:43,061 --> 00:39:47,633
 ♪ Your happiness is overdue ♪

586
00:39:47,666 --> 00:39:49,168
 ♪ I've been dreaming of ♪

587
00:39:49,201 --> 00:39:50,903
 ♪ Dream ♪
 ♪ The skies above ♪

588
00:39:50,936 --> 00:39:54,039
 ♪ Dancing through the stars
With you ♪

589
00:39:54,072 --> 00:39:58,444
 ♪ Oh, take me to ♪

590
00:39:58,477 --> 00:40:01,046
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

591
00:40:01,079 --> 00:40:02,681
 ♪ Is where I want to be ♪

592
00:40:02,714 --> 00:40:05,050
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

593
00:40:05,083 --> 00:40:06,452
 ♪ For you and me ♪

594
00:40:06,485 --> 00:40:09,455
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

595
00:40:09,488 --> 00:40:11,123
 ♪ What you get
Is what you see ♪

596
00:40:11,156 --> 00:40:14,760
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

597
00:40:16,695 --> 00:40:19,164
When is a sandwich
more than a sandwich?

598
00:40:19,197 --> 00:40:23,101
When the sandwich is a meal--
For Team Rocket to steal.

599
00:40:23,134 --> 00:40:24,837
Dinner.
Dinner.

600
00:40:26,972 --> 00:40:28,941
ALL:
Ah!

601
00:40:28,974 --> 00:40:30,843
Huh?

602
00:40:30,876 --> 00:40:32,678
Munch. Munch.

603
00:40:32,711 --> 00:40:34,980
Did that just happen?
Munch. Munch. Munch.

604
00:40:36,114 --> 00:40:37,649
Munch. Munch. Munch.

605
00:40:37,682 --> 00:40:39,685
It's stealing the food
we were stealing.

606
00:40:39,718 --> 00:40:40,986
Oh, no, it's not.

607
00:40:41,019 --> 00:40:42,821
( growls )

608
00:40:42,854 --> 00:40:44,823
Munch. Munch. Munch.
JESSIE: Carry all--

609
00:40:44,856 --> 00:40:47,593
( all grumbling indistinctly )

610
00:40:52,664 --> 00:40:54,767
It's gone.

611
00:40:55,834 --> 00:40:57,503
( ominous theme playing )

612
00:41:12,050 --> 00:41:14,019
( roars )

613
00:41:23,895 --> 00:41:26,198
TORY:
You know, I've never
done that before.

614
00:41:26,231 --> 00:41:27,733
What?

615
00:41:27,766 --> 00:41:30,569
Just playing together
with a big bunch of friends.

616
00:41:30,602 --> 00:41:32,137
Really?
Yeah.

617
00:41:32,170 --> 00:41:34,006
I guess it's because
I've always been

618
00:41:34,039 --> 00:41:36,909
so afraid of Pokémon.

619
00:41:36,942 --> 00:41:40,712
So I'm afraid to get close
to Pokémon trainers too.

620
00:41:40,745 --> 00:41:43,615
Guess I've missed out on a lot.
Hmm.

621
00:41:43,648 --> 00:41:45,784
That means
you're always alone.

622
00:41:45,817 --> 00:41:47,019
Pika.

623
00:41:48,186 --> 00:41:49,688
Pikachu.

624
00:41:49,721 --> 00:41:51,323
But that's all
in the past, right?

625
00:41:51,356 --> 00:41:52,958
Pika.

626
00:41:57,062 --> 00:41:58,531
Hmm.

627
00:42:04,736 --> 00:42:06,672
Corphish!
( screams )

628
00:42:06,705 --> 00:42:08,106
Corphish!
Corphish!

629
00:42:08,139 --> 00:42:09,274
Corphish!

630
00:42:09,307 --> 00:42:11,810
It's okay.

631
00:42:11,843 --> 00:42:14,780
There's no rush.
Okay.

632
00:42:14,813 --> 00:42:16,915
That's Corphish.

633
00:42:16,948 --> 00:42:18,317
Cor...

634
00:42:18,350 --> 00:42:20,920
Pika.
...phish.

635
00:42:23,388 --> 00:42:26,191
TORY:
Come on, guys, there's someone
I want you to meet.

636
00:42:26,224 --> 00:42:27,759
We are we going?

637
00:42:27,792 --> 00:42:29,661
Wherever it is,
I hope there's a kitchen.

638
00:42:29,694 --> 00:42:30,963
( chuckles ):
I'm starving.

639
00:42:37,702 --> 00:42:40,673
 Your passports, please.

640
00:42:42,974 --> 00:42:44,076
 Verified.

641
00:42:45,910 --> 00:42:48,046
My dad's lab
is right over there

642
00:42:48,079 --> 00:42:51,116
so that's why there are so many
security robots all over.

643
00:42:59,658 --> 00:43:00,959
Come on out.

644
00:43:00,992 --> 00:43:05,598
I'm with my new friends.
Come and meet them.

645
00:43:10,001 --> 00:43:13,405
Pika.
So this is your friend, Tory?

646
00:43:13,438 --> 00:43:14,973
But what is it?

647
00:43:15,006 --> 00:43:17,242
It's gorgeous.
And weird.

648
00:43:17,275 --> 00:43:20,379
It's always here for me
whenever I call for it.

649
00:43:20,412 --> 00:43:22,648
Yesterday,
I played with all these guys

650
00:43:22,681 --> 00:43:24,082
and their Pokémon too.

651
00:43:24,115 --> 00:43:25,350
ALL:
Wow!

652
00:43:25,383 --> 00:43:27,319
Wow, Tory, that's so cool.

653
00:43:27,352 --> 00:43:29,221
And it even understands
what I say.

654
00:43:29,254 --> 00:43:30,889
MAY:
Is it a Pokémon?

655
00:43:30,922 --> 00:43:32,658
MAX:
Not one that I've ever seen.

656
00:43:32,691 --> 00:43:34,760
This is just fascinating.

657
00:43:34,793 --> 00:43:37,262
What do you say
I introduce my Pokémon to it?

658
00:43:37,295 --> 00:43:39,198
Go!

659
00:43:41,266 --> 00:43:42,401
Blaze.

660
00:43:42,434 --> 00:43:44,002
Yeah, mine too.

661
00:43:44,035 --> 00:43:45,671
BOTH:
Don't forget ours.

662
00:43:47,439 --> 00:43:49,274
Masquerain.
Blastoise.

663
00:43:49,307 --> 00:43:51,877
Now, let me introduce mine.

664
00:43:53,311 --> 00:43:54,746
Metagross.

665
00:43:54,779 --> 00:43:57,015
A Metagross. Awesome.

666
00:43:57,048 --> 00:43:58,183
Meta.

667
00:43:58,216 --> 00:44:00,185
Pika.
( giggles )

668
00:44:02,487 --> 00:44:04,189
Blast.
Blaze.

669
00:44:06,891 --> 00:44:08,694
Whoa.
( all chuckling )

670
00:44:12,063 --> 00:44:14,166
I got you!

671
00:44:14,199 --> 00:44:16,868
Missed it.

672
00:44:16,901 --> 00:44:18,403
Pika.

673
00:44:18,436 --> 00:44:20,305
Pi--
Whoa!

674
00:44:20,338 --> 00:44:21,907
Oh!
Pi--

675
00:44:23,508 --> 00:44:25,811
( wind roaring )

676
00:44:30,482 --> 00:44:32,918
( howls )

677
00:44:36,221 --> 00:44:37,189
( emergency alarm beeps )

678
00:44:37,222 --> 00:44:39,758
Unidentified object
approaching the building.

679
00:44:39,791 --> 00:44:42,094
Can you
analyze it, please?

680
00:44:43,361 --> 00:44:45,163
It appears to be a Rayquaza.

681
00:44:45,196 --> 00:44:46,097
Rayquaza?

682
00:44:46,131 --> 00:44:49,234
Contact Professor Lund now.
MAN: Right.

683
00:44:53,071 --> 00:44:56,208
Professor, how could a Rayquaza
be coming here?

684
00:44:56,241 --> 00:44:57,743
I don't know.

685
00:44:57,776 --> 00:44:59,811
But for it to leave
the ozone layer again,

686
00:44:59,844 --> 00:45:02,247
there must be
a powerful reason.

687
00:45:03,882 --> 00:45:05,718
( computers beeping )

688
00:45:09,220 --> 00:45:11,323
Do you see that?

689
00:45:11,356 --> 00:45:12,491
I'll magnify it.

690
00:45:12,524 --> 00:45:14,827
( suspenseful theme playing )

691
00:45:15,994 --> 00:45:17,362
That's what I thought.

692
00:45:17,395 --> 00:45:19,364
It's Deoxys.

693
00:45:19,397 --> 00:45:21,734
( ominous theme playing )

694
00:45:31,476 --> 00:45:33,044
COMPUTER:
 System malfunction.

695
00:45:33,077 --> 00:45:35,814
 Losing regulatory control.

696
00:45:38,950 --> 00:45:40,352
LUND:
 Rayquaza must have come here

697
00:45:40,385 --> 00:45:43,121
 after sensing that Deoxys
was here as well.

698
00:45:43,154 --> 00:45:45,791
 If those two battle it out
in our city,

699
00:45:45,824 --> 00:45:47,292
 the result
will be catastrophic.

700
00:45:47,325 --> 00:45:50,395
 Evacuate Larousse City
immediately.

701
00:45:50,428 --> 00:45:53,098
Right away, sir.

702
00:45:53,131 --> 00:45:56,034
Initiating
emergency evacuation.

703
00:45:59,070 --> 00:46:00,338
JENNY ( over P.A. ):
 Fellow citizens,

704
00:46:00,371 --> 00:46:02,974
 we are facing
an emergency situation.

705
00:46:03,007 --> 00:46:05,010
 Please evacuate immediately.

706
00:46:05,043 --> 00:46:07,546
( indistinct chattering )

707
00:46:07,579 --> 00:46:08,947
MAN:
It's party time.

708
00:46:08,980 --> 00:46:11,082
 Please be patient.

709
00:46:11,115 --> 00:46:13,952
 The next ferry
will arrive shortly.

710
00:46:18,356 --> 00:46:20,359
( indistinct chattering )

711
00:46:24,062 --> 00:46:26,331
( alarm blaring )

712
00:46:29,934 --> 00:46:33,305
What's that?
It sounds like the police.

713
00:46:33,338 --> 00:46:34,940
ALL:
Huh?

714
00:46:38,076 --> 00:46:39,578
Tory's out in the garden.

715
00:46:39,611 --> 00:46:42,080
I have to go out
and get him.

716
00:46:42,113 --> 00:46:44,249
Everyone,
evacuate immediately.

717
00:46:44,282 --> 00:46:45,384
Right.

718
00:46:52,891 --> 00:46:54,593
Why won't your
passport work?

719
00:46:54,626 --> 00:46:56,161
This never happens.

720
00:46:56,194 --> 00:46:57,929
Maybe, the system
is shutting down.

721
00:46:57,962 --> 00:47:00,098
( all gasp )

722
00:47:01,466 --> 00:47:03,201
Huh?

723
00:47:03,234 --> 00:47:05,270
It stopped.

724
00:47:05,303 --> 00:47:06,471
 Rebooting.

725
00:47:06,504 --> 00:47:08,207
( grunts )

726
00:47:14,345 --> 00:47:16,147
( grunts )

727
00:47:16,180 --> 00:47:17,148
MAN:
Hey!

728
00:47:17,181 --> 00:47:18,851
( speaking indistinctly )

729
00:47:34,599 --> 00:47:37,302
WOMAN 1: It's moving.
WOMAN 2: Where are we going?

730
00:47:37,335 --> 00:47:38,904
( girl gasps )

731
00:47:38,937 --> 00:47:41,973
WOMAN 3: Excuse me.
MAN: Watch it.

732
00:47:42,006 --> 00:47:44,409
( screams )

733
00:47:47,312 --> 00:47:49,247
Professor Lund.

734
00:47:49,280 --> 00:47:51,249
Ah.

735
00:47:51,282 --> 00:47:52,918
MEOWTH:
Oh, some vacation

736
00:47:52,951 --> 00:47:54,119
this turned out to be.

737
00:47:54,152 --> 00:47:56,221
JESSIE:
Whose bad idea was this?

738
00:47:56,254 --> 00:47:58,189
JAMES:
Let's just say Meowth and I
were overruled.

739
00:47:58,222 --> 00:47:59,491
JESSIE AND MEOWTH:
Huh?

740
00:48:11,436 --> 00:48:13,272
Hey!

741
00:48:14,706 --> 00:48:17,042
( suspenseful theme playing )

742
00:48:20,979 --> 00:48:22,380
What's happening here?

743
00:48:22,413 --> 00:48:25,317
Those things
are carrying people away.

744
00:48:25,350 --> 00:48:28,586
Deoxys, why are you doing
this to us?

745
00:48:28,619 --> 00:48:30,422
( Raybuaza howls )
Huh?

746
00:48:30,455 --> 00:48:32,424
( roars )

747
00:48:51,743 --> 00:48:53,311
The force field.

748
00:48:53,344 --> 00:48:55,480
( dramatic theme playing )

749
00:49:08,159 --> 00:49:09,461
COMPUTER:
 Losing power.

750
00:49:09,494 --> 00:49:12,497
 All systems
will now shut down.

751
00:49:22,106 --> 00:49:23,508
( roars )

752
00:49:40,091 --> 00:49:42,627
( roaring )

753
00:49:42,660 --> 00:49:44,997
( grunts )

754
00:49:47,665 --> 00:49:51,302
Blastoise. Blas--

755
00:49:51,335 --> 00:49:54,306
Blastoise.

756
00:49:55,406 --> 00:49:57,342
Blastoise.

757
00:49:57,375 --> 00:49:58,610
( grunts )

758
00:49:58,643 --> 00:50:01,112
BOTH:
You got it.

759
00:50:01,145 --> 00:50:03,015
Hold on a sec.

760
00:50:07,552 --> 00:50:08,787
It's multiplying.

761
00:50:08,820 --> 00:50:11,623
What is that thing?
Deoxys.

762
00:50:11,656 --> 00:50:12,791
You know its name?

763
00:50:12,824 --> 00:50:14,125
You guys, come back.

764
00:50:14,158 --> 00:50:15,660
ALL:
Huh?

765
00:50:15,693 --> 00:50:17,562
( all gasp )

766
00:50:17,595 --> 00:50:19,264
No, May, look out.

767
00:50:19,297 --> 00:50:20,832
Hey, what do you want?

768
00:50:20,865 --> 00:50:23,368
Blastoise,
use Hydro Pump. Go!

769
00:50:23,401 --> 00:50:25,237
Blastoise!

770
00:50:30,408 --> 00:50:33,445
Blastoise.
Put me down.

771
00:50:33,478 --> 00:50:36,281
Blastoise! Blast!

772
00:50:36,314 --> 00:50:39,418
Sid, no!
May, get in here.

773
00:50:40,318 --> 00:50:43,421
Blaziken, use Flamethrower.

774
00:50:43,454 --> 00:50:46,424
Blaze.

775
00:50:46,457 --> 00:50:48,460
ASH:
Pikachu, Thunderbolt.

776
00:50:48,493 --> 00:50:50,562
PIKACHU:
Pikachu!

777
00:50:53,131 --> 00:50:54,866
Tory, is there
another way out?

778
00:50:54,899 --> 00:50:57,368
Yeah, there is
an underground exit.

779
00:50:57,401 --> 00:50:59,704
Can you show us?
Yes, follow me.

780
00:50:59,737 --> 00:51:01,840
Everyone, let's go.

781
00:51:01,873 --> 00:51:04,609
( suspenseful theme playing )

782
00:51:04,642 --> 00:51:07,212
Blaze!

783
00:51:08,379 --> 00:51:10,115
( screams )

784
00:51:10,915 --> 00:51:12,450
Blaze!

785
00:51:12,483 --> 00:51:15,120
Way to go, Rafe.
All in a day's work.

786
00:51:19,223 --> 00:51:20,492
What do they want?

787
00:51:28,533 --> 00:51:29,567
Let's hurry.

788
00:51:29,600 --> 00:51:32,604
Come on, Brock, it's open.
Okay.

789
00:51:32,637 --> 00:51:35,474
All right, Ash, Rafe,
we gotta go.

790
00:51:36,941 --> 00:51:39,477
Pikachu.
Pika.

791
00:51:39,510 --> 00:51:41,313
( grunts )

792
00:51:42,613 --> 00:51:44,616
Blaze.

793
00:51:44,649 --> 00:51:46,351
Guys, this way.

794
00:51:51,355 --> 00:51:53,592
( panting )
Pika?

795
00:51:55,359 --> 00:51:56,528
Pika!
( all grunt )

796
00:51:56,561 --> 00:51:58,930
Pikachu,
use Thunderbolt now.

797
00:51:58,963 --> 00:52:01,533
Pikachu!

798
00:52:03,401 --> 00:52:07,505
Thanks, Pikachu.
Good Thunderbolt.

799
00:52:07,538 --> 00:52:09,474
Ash, what are you doing?
Let's go.

800
00:52:09,507 --> 00:52:11,443
This is the way
to get out of here.

801
00:52:19,917 --> 00:52:21,819
Wonder where we are now.

802
00:52:21,852 --> 00:52:23,922
It seems to be safe.

803
00:52:23,955 --> 00:52:25,256
There you are.

804
00:52:25,289 --> 00:52:27,559
TORY:
It's Yuko.

805
00:52:29,293 --> 00:52:32,297
( Pokémon chattering )

806
00:52:33,531 --> 00:52:35,467
( panting )

807
00:52:40,004 --> 00:52:41,673
Munch.

808
00:52:44,942 --> 00:52:46,478
Munch?

809
00:52:47,645 --> 00:52:49,948
Munch. Munch.

810
00:52:49,981 --> 00:52:51,683
Munch.

811
00:52:51,716 --> 00:52:53,818
( wind gusting )

812
00:52:53,851 --> 00:52:55,587
( Rayquaza howls )

813
00:52:55,620 --> 00:52:57,789
( Rayquaza roars )

814
00:53:01,592 --> 00:53:02,961
POLICEWOMAN:
Professor, take a look

815
00:53:02,994 --> 00:53:05,230
at all of these people
shown here.

816
00:53:05,263 --> 00:53:07,332
Their evacuation
hasn't been confirmed

817
00:53:07,365 --> 00:53:09,968
at any
of the passport checkpoints.

818
00:53:10,001 --> 00:53:11,469
I'm afraid that could mean

819
00:53:11,502 --> 00:53:13,004
they're still stuck
in Larousse.

820
00:53:13,037 --> 00:53:14,806
( grunts )

821
00:53:19,477 --> 00:53:21,613
The entire town is enclosed
within a force field.

822
00:53:21,646 --> 00:53:25,250
It's impossible for anyone
to come in or to leave.

823
00:53:25,283 --> 00:53:26,851
All communication
with the outside

824
00:53:26,884 --> 00:53:28,353
is jammed as well.

825
00:53:28,386 --> 00:53:30,321
They've switched
to backup generators,

826
00:53:30,354 --> 00:53:32,457
but all systems
are still down.

827
00:53:32,490 --> 00:53:34,692
Even the Poké Ball
Management System

828
00:53:34,725 --> 00:53:35,893
isn't functioning.

829
00:53:35,926 --> 00:53:37,528
Yeah, it won't work.

830
00:53:37,561 --> 00:53:39,697
How can we call out
our Pokémon?

831
00:53:39,730 --> 00:53:41,032
Guess we can't.

832
00:53:41,065 --> 00:53:44,402
Hey, Tory,
what did you call that thing?

833
00:53:44,435 --> 00:53:46,004
Was it Deoxys?
Hmm-mm.

834
00:53:46,037 --> 00:53:47,372
That's right.

835
00:53:47,405 --> 00:53:49,774
A Pokémon from outer space.

836
00:53:49,807 --> 00:53:51,309
What?

837
00:53:51,342 --> 00:53:53,845
Four years ago,
a meteorite came down

838
00:53:53,878 --> 00:53:55,313
and struck the North Pole.

839
00:53:55,346 --> 00:53:57,282
And located inside of it

840
00:53:57,315 --> 00:53:58,883
was a completely
unknown Pokémon.

841
00:53:58,916 --> 00:54:01,819
 It was Professor Lund
who gave that Pokémon

842
00:54:01,852 --> 00:54:03,354
 the name Deoxys.

843
00:54:03,387 --> 00:54:04,622
( roaring )

844
00:54:04,655 --> 00:54:06,357
 But then almost
immediately,

845
00:54:06,390 --> 00:54:08,026
 Rayquaza appeared
from the ozone

846
00:54:08,059 --> 00:54:09,527
 and attacked Deoxys.

847
00:54:11,762 --> 00:54:14,632
( roars )

848
00:54:14,665 --> 00:54:16,801
 Apparently,
Rayquaza was threatened

849
00:54:16,834 --> 00:54:19,671
 and thought Deoxys
was invading its territory.

850
00:54:19,704 --> 00:54:23,708
 Deoxys vanished deep
into the sea.

851
00:54:25,943 --> 00:54:29,013
BROCK:
I don't get it. How could it be
the same Deoxys?

852
00:54:29,046 --> 00:54:30,782
After getting beaten
by Rayquaza,

853
00:54:30,815 --> 00:54:33,751
Deoxys must have slowly
been regenerating.

854
00:54:33,784 --> 00:54:34,919
Regenerating?

855
00:54:34,952 --> 00:54:36,387
That's right,

856
00:54:36,420 --> 00:54:38,389
it has astounding
regenerative powers.

857
00:54:38,422 --> 00:54:40,391
And that's
what Professor Lund and I

858
00:54:40,424 --> 00:54:41,826
have been studying
all these years.

859
00:54:47,598 --> 00:54:50,535
REBECCA:
It sounds more
like science fiction.

860
00:54:50,568 --> 00:54:52,804
This is something
I'd love to research.

861
00:54:52,837 --> 00:54:55,606
But I wonder if
it could somehow get in

862
00:54:55,639 --> 00:54:57,375
through a crack in the wall.

863
00:54:58,109 --> 00:54:59,577
Knock it off, Max.

864
00:54:59,610 --> 00:55:01,412
Yeah, stop scaring us
right now.

865
00:55:01,445 --> 00:55:02,914
( laughing ):
Just kidding.

866
00:55:02,947 --> 00:55:05,416
There's no way it's coming in
through a crack.

867
00:55:05,449 --> 00:55:07,352
( door opens )
What was that?

868
00:55:07,385 --> 00:55:09,420
Come on, Blaziken.

869
00:55:09,453 --> 00:55:10,655
Blaze. Blaze.

870
00:55:10,688 --> 00:55:13,524
( suspenseful theme playing )

871
00:55:13,557 --> 00:55:15,694
( clanging and rumbling )

872
00:55:19,830 --> 00:55:22,367
Blaze.
Pika.

873
00:55:25,069 --> 00:55:27,004
( both chattering )

874
00:55:27,037 --> 00:55:28,740
Oh!
Pika!

875
00:55:34,078 --> 00:55:35,580
Munch.

876
00:55:36,480 --> 00:55:37,648
Hey, that's the Pokémon

877
00:55:37,681 --> 00:55:39,651
that ate every bite
of our food.

878
00:55:40,751 --> 00:55:42,887
Are you stuck in there,
Munchlax?

879
00:55:42,920 --> 00:55:44,889
Let's see.

880
00:55:44,922 --> 00:55:46,891
( grunting )

881
00:55:50,194 --> 00:55:51,596
Our sandwiches.

882
00:55:51,629 --> 00:55:53,898
Everything
but the peanut butter. Hmm.

883
00:55:53,931 --> 00:55:56,968
And, of course,
that one was mine.

884
00:55:59,904 --> 00:56:01,539
Hold on. Hold on.

885
00:56:05,009 --> 00:56:09,381
Okay, please just don't come
any closer, you two.

886
00:56:10,915 --> 00:56:13,418
Pika. Pikachu.

887
00:56:15,085 --> 00:56:17,121
Munch.
( sighs )

888
00:56:17,154 --> 00:56:19,924
I'm so hungry.
So am I.

889
00:56:19,957 --> 00:56:21,726
Me too.
Mu--

890
00:56:21,759 --> 00:56:22,894
Mu--?

891
00:56:22,927 --> 00:56:24,028
Munchlax.

892
00:56:24,061 --> 00:56:25,563
Really? I can have it?

893
00:56:25,596 --> 00:56:27,966
Munch. Munch. Munch.

894
00:56:31,135 --> 00:56:33,871
ALL: No, thanks.
Munch.

895
00:56:33,904 --> 00:56:36,941
( all gasp and sigh )

896
00:56:45,149 --> 00:56:47,518
BROCK:
We have to find food and water
right away.

897
00:56:47,551 --> 00:56:51,489
Great. And I'll try and find out
where those people were taken.

898
00:56:51,522 --> 00:56:54,091
Yuko, take care
of my sisters, please.

899
00:56:54,124 --> 00:56:56,694
Of course,
but don't you worry about us.

900
00:56:56,727 --> 00:56:58,062
You take care of yourselves.

901
00:56:58,095 --> 00:56:59,530
RAFE:
We will.

902
00:56:59,563 --> 00:57:01,633
ASH:
All right, let's go.

903
00:57:05,970 --> 00:57:09,207
Munchlax.

904
00:57:09,240 --> 00:57:11,742
Munchlax.

905
00:57:11,775 --> 00:57:14,045
( indistinct chattering )

906
00:57:14,078 --> 00:57:16,014
( sighs )

907
00:57:17,615 --> 00:57:19,217
I'm worried, Max.

908
00:57:19,250 --> 00:57:22,153
I really hope
they're all okay.

909
00:57:22,186 --> 00:57:23,554
Yeah, me too.

910
00:57:23,587 --> 00:57:25,556
I wish they'd hurry
and come back.

911
00:57:25,589 --> 00:57:27,625
( speaks indistinctly
)

912
00:57:34,031 --> 00:57:36,634
Still no good.
Nothing's happening.

913
00:57:36,667 --> 00:57:38,970
Yeah. It must be tied
into the town's system.

914
00:57:39,003 --> 00:57:40,705
I can see the food
in there too.

915
00:57:40,738 --> 00:57:43,274
We just need to figure out
a way to break in.

916
00:57:43,307 --> 00:57:45,109
Pika. Pika.
Hmm?            Hmm?

917
00:57:45,142 --> 00:57:48,012
Pikachu!

918
00:57:54,051 --> 00:57:55,186
It worked.

919
00:57:55,219 --> 00:57:57,755
Pikachu, great idea.
Pikachu.

920
00:57:58,856 --> 00:58:01,926
Whoa, gotta catch them all.

921
00:58:01,959 --> 00:58:04,896
Pika.

922
00:58:04,929 --> 00:58:08,132
Pikachu. Pika?

923
00:58:08,165 --> 00:58:10,601
Huh? What is it, Pikachu?

924
00:58:10,634 --> 00:58:11,903
( all gasp )

925
00:58:14,572 --> 00:58:16,007
Look out!
Run!

926
00:58:16,040 --> 00:58:17,509
Pika!

927
00:58:21,178 --> 00:58:23,548
Pika!
Look out!

928
00:58:27,151 --> 00:58:28,286
Plusle. Minun.

929
00:58:28,319 --> 00:58:30,054
( both screaming )

930
00:58:31,822 --> 00:58:33,157
ASH: Put me down!
BROCK: Let go!

931
00:58:33,190 --> 00:58:36,060
( grunts )

932
00:58:38,095 --> 00:58:40,565
Pikachu!

933
00:58:40,598 --> 00:58:42,099
( all grunts )

934
00:58:42,132 --> 00:58:45,036
No!
( whimpers )

935
00:58:45,069 --> 00:58:47,838
( screaming )

936
00:58:47,871 --> 00:58:50,575
Pika.
( gasps )

937
00:58:53,077 --> 00:58:55,713
Here they all come, guys.
Pika.

938
00:58:55,746 --> 00:58:57,815
Come on, Tory,
let's go.

939
00:59:03,020 --> 00:59:05,156
( suspenseful theme playing )

940
00:59:18,702 --> 00:59:20,304
Looks like they're all gone.

941
00:59:20,337 --> 00:59:22,574
That was close.

942
00:59:23,707 --> 00:59:25,776
Oh, Plusle.

943
00:59:25,809 --> 00:59:27,678
It's all my fault.

944
00:59:27,711 --> 00:59:30,047
I should've.

945
00:59:30,080 --> 00:59:32,016
( sighs )

946
00:59:35,152 --> 00:59:36,621
I'm sorry.

947
00:59:36,654 --> 00:59:38,823
Pika. Pika. Pika.

948
00:59:38,856 --> 00:59:40,658
Pikachu.

949
00:59:42,359 --> 00:59:44,061
BROCK:
Ash,

950
00:59:44,094 --> 00:59:46,697
look what I just found.

951
00:59:46,730 --> 00:59:49,934
Precious water.
ASH: All right!

952
00:59:57,875 --> 00:59:59,343
RAFE:
Okay, so that's where

953
00:59:59,376 --> 01:00:01,779
they're holding everyone
captive.

954
01:00:01,812 --> 01:00:04,415
I guess,
but what in the world for?

955
01:00:04,448 --> 01:00:06,183
ROBOT:
 Release immediately.

956
01:00:06,216 --> 01:00:08,719
 Release immediately.

957
01:00:08,752 --> 01:00:11,288
( weakened ):
 Release immediately.

958
01:00:11,321 --> 01:00:15,026
 Release immediate--

959
01:00:20,431 --> 01:00:22,867
It let go.

960
01:00:22,900 --> 01:00:24,636
But why?

961
01:00:30,774 --> 01:00:33,745
( Rayquaza howls )

962
01:00:40,350 --> 01:00:42,654
( all snoring )

963
01:00:51,729 --> 01:00:53,230
Hmm, go back.

964
01:00:53,263 --> 01:00:55,266
Let me just take
another look at that.

965
01:00:55,299 --> 01:00:56,768
Sure.

966
01:01:01,338 --> 01:01:02,873
Surskit. Surskit.

967
01:01:02,906 --> 01:01:05,910
What is it? What's wrong?

968
01:01:08,512 --> 01:01:10,815
Pika.

969
01:01:10,848 --> 01:01:12,216
( object clatters )
Blaze?

970
01:01:22,960 --> 01:01:25,329
( both scream )
Let's get out of here.

971
01:01:25,362 --> 01:01:27,965
YOKU:
Yes, there's an underground
laboratory.

972
01:01:27,998 --> 01:01:30,334
Let's go. Follow me.

973
01:01:30,367 --> 01:01:32,203
MAX: Munchlax.
Munch?

974
01:01:32,236 --> 01:01:33,871
Munch. Munch. Munch.

975
01:01:38,008 --> 01:01:40,478
Try and stay calm.
Now go.

976
01:01:40,511 --> 01:01:42,814
( dramatic theme playing )

977
01:02:01,131 --> 01:02:03,834
We should be safe down here
for the time being.

978
01:02:03,867 --> 01:02:06,204
RAFE: That's good.
BLAZE: Blaze. Blaze.

979
01:02:08,238 --> 01:02:09,874
Pika.

980
01:02:13,010 --> 01:02:14,178
ASH:
What's this?

981
01:02:14,211 --> 01:02:15,946
YOKU:
The lab where we studied Deoxys

982
01:02:15,979 --> 01:02:17,448
and its regeneration.

983
01:02:17,481 --> 01:02:20,017
There were actually two
of them before.

984
01:02:20,050 --> 01:02:21,886
Rayquaza defeated one

985
01:02:21,919 --> 01:02:24,321
while the other Deoxys
was still dormant

986
01:02:24,354 --> 01:02:25,990
inside of this meteorite.

987
01:02:26,023 --> 01:02:27,391
TERESA:
So then you're saying that--

988
01:02:27,424 --> 01:02:29,393
YOKU:
Yes. That crystal,

989
01:02:29,426 --> 01:02:31,095
it's a part of Deoxys.

990
01:02:31,128 --> 01:02:32,530
Part of--

991
01:02:32,563 --> 01:02:34,999
What do you mean?
Pika.

992
01:02:38,268 --> 01:02:39,370
( all gasp )

993
01:02:44,441 --> 01:02:45,943
Pika.

994
01:02:48,078 --> 01:02:50,447
What?
Hey, Tory, it's your friend.

995
01:02:50,480 --> 01:02:52,283
Pika.

996
01:02:52,316 --> 01:02:55,419
Wait a second.
Then Tory's friend is--

997
01:02:55,452 --> 01:02:57,421
Right. It's Deoxys.

998
01:02:57,454 --> 01:02:58,923
( all gasp )

999
01:03:14,404 --> 01:03:15,973
Huh?

1000
01:03:16,006 --> 01:03:18,810
That's it.
It all makes sense.

1001
01:03:20,978 --> 01:03:23,881
This is Tory's friend's
light pattern.

1002
01:03:25,215 --> 01:03:27,518
And this is the pattern
of the aurora

1003
01:03:27,551 --> 01:03:29,920
that covered Larousse.

1004
01:03:29,953 --> 01:03:31,322
It's the same.

1005
01:03:31,355 --> 01:03:33,924
Yeah, I think it might be
how they communicate.

1006
01:03:33,957 --> 01:03:37,561
Oh, I see.
So can you tell what it says?

1007
01:03:37,594 --> 01:03:40,965
TERESA:
Well, let's start
with the green pattern.

1008
01:03:42,332 --> 01:03:45,069
This one means friend.

1009
01:03:45,102 --> 01:03:47,304
And this one seems
to be asking,

1010
01:03:47,337 --> 01:03:49,240
"Where are you?"

1011
01:03:49,273 --> 01:03:51,342
So it's just looking
for its friend?

1012
01:03:51,375 --> 01:03:52,209
Pika.

1013
01:03:52,243 --> 01:03:54,478
YOKU:
Of course. Deoxys carried off

1014
01:03:54,511 --> 01:03:57,615
all those people and Pokémon
because they were interfering

1015
01:03:57,648 --> 01:03:59,550
while it searched
for its friend.

1016
01:03:59,583 --> 01:04:01,352
What?
Deoxys sees certain types

1017
01:04:01,385 --> 01:04:02,486
of electrical fields.

1018
01:04:02,519 --> 01:04:04,588
But it's not only
electrical devices

1019
01:04:04,621 --> 01:04:07,358
that give off those fields,
so do people and Pokémon,

1020
01:04:07,391 --> 01:04:11,262
and they were blocking
its vision.

1021
01:04:11,295 --> 01:04:13,898
That's why it's moving them
out of the way,

1022
01:04:13,931 --> 01:04:15,333
to find it.

1023
01:04:18,168 --> 01:04:21,138
( dramatic theme playing )

1024
01:04:42,059 --> 01:04:44,362
( gasps and sighs )

1025
01:04:52,703 --> 01:04:58,542
Please, Yuko, you've got
to help this Deoxys regenerate.

1026
01:04:58,575 --> 01:05:00,277
It's so sad.

1027
01:05:00,310 --> 01:05:02,346
It's been alone
all of this time.

1028
01:05:02,379 --> 01:05:06,984
You're right. Once Deoxys finds
its friend, it'll go back home.

1029
01:05:07,017 --> 01:05:08,319
Pikachu.
But the problem is,

1030
01:05:08,352 --> 01:05:10,220
the emergency power
we're running on now

1031
01:05:10,253 --> 01:05:13,157
isn't nearly enough necessary
to operate this device.

1032
01:05:13,190 --> 01:05:16,160
If it's electricity you want,
then I'm your guy.

1033
01:05:16,193 --> 01:05:18,228
I can get
the wind generators going.

1034
01:05:18,261 --> 01:05:19,596
Can we help?
Can we help?

1035
01:05:19,629 --> 01:05:21,265
Yes, we'll need everyone's help

1036
01:05:21,298 --> 01:05:23,033
to save those people
and Pokémon.

1037
01:05:23,066 --> 01:05:24,468
Let's start working
on a plan,

1038
01:05:24,501 --> 01:05:26,670
and then we'll go out
to where they're being held.

1039
01:05:26,703 --> 01:05:28,539
I'll zero in on it.

1040
01:05:29,639 --> 01:05:31,041
That's where they all are.

1041
01:05:31,074 --> 01:05:33,110
ASH:
Great. Let's go get them, guys.

1042
01:05:33,143 --> 01:05:34,378
ALL:
All right!

1043
01:05:34,411 --> 01:05:38,549
( suspenseful theme playing )

1044
01:05:42,519 --> 01:05:44,488
( all chattering )

1045
01:05:53,530 --> 01:05:55,532
( panting )

1046
01:05:55,565 --> 01:05:59,403
I'll never take an escalator
for granted again.

1047
01:06:14,117 --> 01:06:16,087
( grunts )

1048
01:06:18,555 --> 01:06:22,526
Deoxys, we're not your enemies.
We're your friends.

1049
01:06:25,062 --> 01:06:26,330
If you'll just trust us,

1050
01:06:26,363 --> 01:06:28,599
we can help you
find your friend. I promise.

1051
01:06:33,103 --> 01:06:35,439
Blaziken, use Flamethrower now.

1052
01:06:40,343 --> 01:06:44,048
Pikachu, Thunderbolt him.
Pikachu!

1053
01:06:47,317 --> 01:06:51,088
Metagross, use Reflector.

1054
01:06:51,121 --> 01:06:52,389
Meta!

1055
01:06:52,422 --> 01:06:54,191
TERESA:
Quick, now's our chance.

1056
01:06:54,224 --> 01:06:56,027
TORY:
This way.

1057
01:06:59,162 --> 01:07:01,331
Now, Overheat.

1058
01:07:01,364 --> 01:07:02,466
Blaze!

1059
01:07:04,868 --> 01:07:06,770
You okay?

1060
01:07:06,803 --> 01:07:09,473
We're fine, Ash.
Just go on.

1061
01:07:09,506 --> 01:07:11,675
Rafe can handle it.

1062
01:07:11,708 --> 01:07:15,145
Just don't let anything happen
to my sisters, Ash.

1063
01:07:15,178 --> 01:07:18,082
You can count on that.

1064
01:07:19,449 --> 01:07:22,420
Blaziken, Overheat!
Blaze.

1065
01:07:27,791 --> 01:07:30,327
( roars )

1066
01:07:46,910 --> 01:07:49,880
Rayquaza has broken through.

1067
01:07:49,913 --> 01:07:51,382
What have I done?

1068
01:07:59,489 --> 01:08:02,392
Blaze....

1069
01:08:02,425 --> 01:08:04,528
Relax, Blaziken.
Blaze.

1070
01:08:12,469 --> 01:08:14,438
( roars )

1071
01:08:39,663 --> 01:08:41,599
( all chattering )

1072
01:08:42,699 --> 01:08:44,668
( roars )

1073
01:08:45,869 --> 01:08:47,638
Rayquaza.
Now what's that?

1074
01:08:47,671 --> 01:08:49,673
( roaring )

1075
01:09:01,918 --> 01:09:05,389
All right, now let's do it
just like we planned. Okay guys?

1076
01:09:05,422 --> 01:09:06,523
BROCK:
Got you.

1077
01:09:06,556 --> 01:09:08,559
TERESA:
We're with you, Ash.

1078
01:09:10,994 --> 01:09:12,930
Munch. Munch. Munch.

1079
01:09:12,963 --> 01:09:14,665
Munchlax.

1080
01:09:14,698 --> 01:09:17,201
Come on, there's no time for you
to go back for it.

1081
01:09:17,234 --> 01:09:19,203
Oh, Munchlax!

1082
01:09:26,743 --> 01:09:28,912
You ready?
Just about.

1083
01:09:28,945 --> 01:09:30,547
All we need
is the electricity.

1084
01:09:30,580 --> 01:09:33,817
But if we had that,
we wouldn't need to fix it.

1085
01:09:33,850 --> 01:09:36,353
What are they doing over there?

1086
01:09:36,386 --> 01:09:39,323
I'm hoping he pulls a sandwich
out of that box.

1087
01:09:39,356 --> 01:09:42,292
From your lips,
to my stomach.

1088
01:09:42,325 --> 01:09:43,694
ASH:
You guys,

1089
01:09:43,727 --> 01:09:45,729
we've come to help you.

1090
01:09:45,762 --> 01:09:47,965
Hey, Ash, we're up here.

1091
01:09:47,998 --> 01:09:50,000
You got Pikachu
and Plusle, right?

1092
01:09:50,033 --> 01:09:52,436
Yeah. We're all set.

1093
01:09:52,469 --> 01:09:53,604
Pika.

1094
01:09:54,738 --> 01:09:56,707
( Rayquaza roars )

1095
01:10:00,910 --> 01:10:03,714
( suspenseful theme playing )

1096
01:10:20,664 --> 01:10:22,633
( roars )

1097
01:10:34,644 --> 01:10:36,614
( growls )

1098
01:10:40,650 --> 01:10:42,619
ASH: Pikachu.
TORY: Plusle.

1099
01:10:42,652 --> 01:10:44,388
BOTH:
Thunderbolt, now.

1100
01:10:48,058 --> 01:10:49,893
SID:
There's your electricity.

1101
01:10:49,926 --> 01:10:52,029
( Pikachu screams )

1102
01:10:52,062 --> 01:10:53,631
That's good. Stop.

1103
01:10:54,731 --> 01:10:57,268
All right.
We're recharged.

1104
01:10:59,936 --> 01:11:01,371
Yeah!

1105
01:11:01,404 --> 01:11:03,407
All right.

1106
01:11:05,942 --> 01:11:08,378
( grunting ):
Ouch.

1107
01:11:08,411 --> 01:11:10,314
( both chattering )

1108
01:11:13,683 --> 01:11:15,319
( both scream )

1109
01:11:22,092 --> 01:11:24,428
You were great, Tory.

1110
01:11:25,162 --> 01:11:27,698
( heroic theme playing )

1111
01:11:33,002 --> 01:11:34,471
( laughs )

1112
01:11:38,842 --> 01:11:40,844
( roars )

1113
01:11:52,756 --> 01:11:54,725
( all panting )

1114
01:11:57,694 --> 01:11:59,730
( roars )

1115
01:12:06,403 --> 01:12:07,905
Let's go.
Yeah.

1116
01:12:11,141 --> 01:12:13,877
( grunts )

1117
01:12:13,910 --> 01:12:15,879
That should do it.

1118
01:12:15,912 --> 01:12:18,382
Coming down!

1119
01:12:18,415 --> 01:12:19,716
( grunts )

1120
01:12:19,749 --> 01:12:21,685
( groans )

1121
01:12:28,892 --> 01:12:31,895
SID:
Hey, May, I'm coming for you.

1122
01:12:31,928 --> 01:12:33,397
Was that Sid?

1123
01:12:33,430 --> 01:12:35,866
BOTH:
Uh, and Rafe!

1124
01:12:35,899 --> 01:12:38,101
May!

1125
01:12:38,134 --> 01:12:39,970
( grunts )

1126
01:12:40,003 --> 01:12:41,671
Gross.

1127
01:12:41,704 --> 01:12:42,840
Metagross.

1128
01:12:44,174 --> 01:12:45,876
Audrey, Kathryn,
you okay?

1129
01:12:45,909 --> 01:12:47,611
KATHRYN: Uh-huh.
AUDREY: We're fine.

1130
01:12:47,644 --> 01:12:49,146
Where's Ash and the others?

1131
01:12:49,179 --> 01:12:50,814
They went back
to the laboratory.

1132
01:12:50,847 --> 01:12:53,917
Okay, are you ready
to get started on this?

1133
01:12:53,950 --> 01:12:55,919
( switches clicking )

1134
01:13:06,796 --> 01:13:08,665
Perfect, the power's
back on.

1135
01:13:08,698 --> 01:13:10,434
Yeah, those guys
pulled it off.

1136
01:13:10,467 --> 01:13:11,735
Mm-hmm.

1137
01:13:19,008 --> 01:13:20,978
( all grunting )

1138
01:13:35,658 --> 01:13:37,828
( all chattering )

1139
01:13:43,032 --> 01:13:45,235
Blaziken. Blaziken.

1140
01:13:45,268 --> 01:13:48,539
Metagross.

1141
01:14:01,284 --> 01:14:03,520
( all groaning )

1142
01:14:03,553 --> 01:14:05,655
My cramp's
getting a cramp.

1143
01:14:05,688 --> 01:14:07,691
We're always spinning
our wheels

1144
01:14:07,724 --> 01:14:10,126
but this is ridiculous.

1145
01:14:10,159 --> 01:14:11,895
Just pedal!

1146
01:14:23,239 --> 01:14:26,243
I'm set. Are you both ready
to use the laser?

1147
01:14:26,276 --> 01:14:29,613
Yes. I think
you should turn it on, Tory.

1148
01:14:29,646 --> 01:14:31,848
It is your friend after all,

1149
01:14:31,881 --> 01:14:33,750
so you should do it.

1150
01:14:38,154 --> 01:14:39,623
Hmm.

1151
01:14:46,029 --> 01:14:47,531
Here goes.

1152
01:14:50,667 --> 01:14:53,704
( dramatic theme playing )

1153
01:15:07,216 --> 01:15:09,786
Pika.

1154
01:15:17,594 --> 01:15:19,663
TORY:
Still no good.

1155
01:15:23,066 --> 01:15:24,334
Oh, no,

1156
01:15:24,367 --> 01:15:26,336
we're still 20 percent short
on energy.

1157
01:15:26,369 --> 01:15:28,305
Wow, we're so close.

1158
01:15:28,338 --> 01:15:29,973
Okay, Pikachu,

1159
01:15:30,006 --> 01:15:32,175
Plusle, Minun,
you know what to do.

1160
01:15:32,208 --> 01:15:33,910
Pika.

1161
01:15:33,943 --> 01:15:37,748
Pikachu!
( both shouting )

1162
01:15:43,086 --> 01:15:45,822
( upbeat theme playing )

1163
01:15:58,001 --> 01:16:00,670
Great idea,
we got just what we need.

1164
01:16:00,703 --> 01:16:02,939
It works.
All right.

1165
01:16:02,972 --> 01:16:05,142
( all shouting )

1166
01:16:16,152 --> 01:16:19,089
( glass shattering )

1167
01:16:19,122 --> 01:16:20,991
( all gasp )

1168
01:16:34,203 --> 01:16:36,206
( dramatic theme playing )

1169
01:16:41,144 --> 01:16:43,380
We did it!

1170
01:16:43,413 --> 01:16:46,717
Oh, Deoxys,
it's really you.

1171
01:16:52,288 --> 01:16:54,224
( chuckles )

1172
01:17:00,163 --> 01:17:01,765
Pika!

1173
01:17:17,947 --> 01:17:20,984
Deoxys, do you wanna go
find your friend now?

1174
01:17:29,292 --> 01:17:31,662
( both laugh )
Pika.

1175
01:17:33,963 --> 01:17:35,065
Pika.

1176
01:17:41,504 --> 01:17:43,073
Pika!

1177
01:17:48,778 --> 01:17:50,681
ASH & TORY:
Whoa!

1178
01:17:57,253 --> 01:17:59,222
( roars )

1179
01:18:13,169 --> 01:18:15,172
( all gasping )

1180
01:18:33,523 --> 01:18:36,960
The force field's gone.
Just like that?

1181
01:18:43,332 --> 01:18:44,835
( roars )

1182
01:18:56,946 --> 01:18:58,949
( heroic theme playing )

1183
01:19:00,883 --> 01:19:02,986
( roaring )

1184
01:19:29,312 --> 01:19:31,314
( whimpers )
Pika.

1185
01:19:44,627 --> 01:19:47,163
( Rayquaza roars )

1186
01:19:47,196 --> 01:19:49,065
( both gasp )
Pika.

1187
01:20:18,928 --> 01:20:23,033
( mellow theme playing )

1188
01:20:52,662 --> 01:20:54,397
( both gasp )
Pika.

1189
01:21:03,072 --> 01:21:04,875
( both chattering )

1190
01:21:24,527 --> 01:21:27,097
( laughing ):
Pika.

1191
01:21:39,008 --> 01:21:40,277
( both gasp )
Pika!

1192
01:21:43,212 --> 01:21:45,348
( suspenseful theme playing )

1193
01:21:58,728 --> 01:22:00,063
Hey, knock it off!

1194
01:22:00,096 --> 01:22:02,198
Stop, Rayquaza.
Pika.

1195
01:22:04,734 --> 01:22:06,202
( roaring )

1196
01:22:31,360 --> 01:22:33,296
( roars )

1197
01:22:37,466 --> 01:22:40,737
 Warning! Warning!
Warning!

1198
01:22:40,770 --> 01:22:44,407
 Danger! Danger! Danger!

1199
01:22:46,409 --> 01:22:49,412
 Evacuate! Evacuate!

1200
01:22:49,445 --> 01:22:50,680
What happened?

1201
01:22:50,713 --> 01:22:53,483
Security somehow started up.

1202
01:23:11,500 --> 01:23:14,170
 Warning! Evacuate!

1203
01:23:14,203 --> 01:23:17,106
 Warning! Evacuate!

1204
01:23:17,139 --> 01:23:18,341
 Warning!

1205
01:23:18,374 --> 01:23:21,110
( weakening ):
 Evacuate.

1206
01:23:21,143 --> 01:23:25,081
 Warning. E-vac-u-ate.

1207
01:23:44,433 --> 01:23:47,103
Somehow security
has gone on overdrive.

1208
01:23:47,136 --> 01:23:48,671
It won't shut down.

1209
01:23:48,704 --> 01:23:49,806
Yuko.

1210
01:23:49,839 --> 01:23:51,441
Professor Lund.

1211
01:23:51,474 --> 01:23:53,309
( roaring )

1212
01:24:26,275 --> 01:24:28,478
Everything's
totally out of control.

1213
01:24:28,511 --> 01:24:29,612
Ash, I'm scared.

1214
01:24:37,620 --> 01:24:39,889
Rayquaza. Deoxys.

1215
01:24:39,922 --> 01:24:41,557
Pika!

1216
01:24:41,590 --> 01:24:43,159
Whoa!

1217
01:24:44,293 --> 01:24:47,130
Plusle. Minun.
Pikachu.

1218
01:24:47,163 --> 01:24:48,297
Pika.

1219
01:24:48,330 --> 01:24:50,133
They almost hit us that time.

1220
01:24:50,166 --> 01:24:51,734
Let's try and get back
to Yuko.

1221
01:24:51,767 --> 01:24:54,403
 Tory, can you hear me? Tory?

1222
01:24:54,436 --> 01:24:55,337
Daddy.

1223
01:24:55,371 --> 01:24:57,707
 You must listen
to me very carefully.

1224
01:24:57,740 --> 01:25:01,244
 As you can see, all the block
robots are malfunctioning.

1225
01:25:01,277 --> 01:25:02,478
The chief robot,

1226
01:25:02,511 --> 01:25:04,247
which controls
all other block robots,

1227
01:25:04,280 --> 01:25:05,648
should be near you.

1228
01:25:05,681 --> 01:25:09,218
We no longer have power
over that robot from the booth.

1229
01:25:09,251 --> 01:25:12,255
Understand?
So here's what you have to do.

1230
01:25:12,288 --> 01:25:14,323
And I need for you to be brave.

1231
01:25:14,356 --> 01:25:16,759
 Tory, do you have
your passport?

1232
01:25:16,792 --> 01:25:19,862
 You must present your passport
to the chief robot.

1233
01:25:19,895 --> 01:25:21,597
 Then everything should unlock

1234
01:25:21,630 --> 01:25:24,233
 but only
for a very brief moment.

1235
01:25:24,266 --> 01:25:25,501
 That should allow us

1236
01:25:25,534 --> 01:25:27,503
 just enough time
to regain control.

1237
01:25:27,536 --> 01:25:30,373
 And shut down
the security system.

1238
01:25:30,406 --> 01:25:32,575
 Block robots are surrounding
the battle tower

1239
01:25:32,608 --> 01:25:35,311
 making any approach by us
impossible.

1240
01:25:35,344 --> 01:25:37,847
 Son, the fate of our town
is in your hands.

1241
01:25:37,880 --> 01:25:40,283
 I know we can count on you--

1242
01:25:46,555 --> 01:25:49,692
ROBOT:
 Warning! Evacuate!

1243
01:25:49,725 --> 01:25:50,893
 Warning!

1244
01:25:50,926 --> 01:25:53,896
( weakening ):
 Eva--

1245
01:25:53,929 --> 01:25:55,565
( suspenseful theme playing )

1246
01:26:02,805 --> 01:26:04,373
Don't you worry, sir.

1247
01:26:04,406 --> 01:26:06,209
Pikachu and I
are gonna help Tory

1248
01:26:06,242 --> 01:26:07,777
save this town together.

1249
01:26:07,810 --> 01:26:09,279
Pika.

1250
01:26:10,546 --> 01:26:12,448
ASH:
We've gotta get to that tower.

1251
01:26:15,284 --> 01:26:18,388
Look at that.
Quick, let's go.

1252
01:26:28,030 --> 01:26:29,899
Okay. Just a little more.

1253
01:26:29,932 --> 01:26:31,434
ALL:
Whoa!

1254
01:26:31,467 --> 01:26:33,970
Munch, Munch, Munch.

1255
01:26:34,003 --> 01:26:36,472
Munchlax?
( all scream )

1256
01:26:46,715 --> 01:26:48,317
Snorlax.

1257
01:26:48,350 --> 01:26:51,354
A Snorlax. That's it.

1258
01:26:53,689 --> 01:26:55,291
Sorry.

1259
01:27:00,729 --> 01:27:01,864
Pika.

1260
01:27:01,897 --> 01:27:03,366
TORY:
Hey, Ash.

1261
01:27:04,933 --> 01:27:07,470
Tory, don't worry.
I'm okay.

1262
01:27:07,503 --> 01:27:09,739
I'll take care of this.

1263
01:27:13,709 --> 01:27:15,544
Pika.

1264
01:27:15,577 --> 01:27:16,679
Pikachu.

1265
01:27:20,582 --> 01:27:21,450
Pika!

1266
01:27:21,483 --> 01:27:25,054
Oh, wow, cool.
I'm right behind you.

1267
01:27:25,087 --> 01:27:27,390
( grunting )

1268
01:27:35,864 --> 01:27:38,434
Pika! Pika!

1269
01:27:47,676 --> 01:27:48,778
No!

1270
01:27:51,080 --> 01:27:53,382
Oh, no.
Pikachu.

1271
01:27:53,415 --> 01:27:54,984
TORY:
Ash!

1272
01:27:55,017 --> 01:27:57,653
Use my passport!
Throw it.

1273
01:27:57,686 --> 01:27:58,821
( grunts )

1274
01:28:05,394 --> 01:28:06,663
Pika.

1275
01:28:09,365 --> 01:28:11,667
Pika.

1276
01:28:11,700 --> 01:28:12,835
Pikachu!

1277
01:28:12,868 --> 01:28:17,373
Pika, Pika. Pikachu.

1278
01:28:35,991 --> 01:28:38,861
This better work.

1279
01:28:40,729 --> 01:28:43,366
COMPUTER:
 Passport has been verified.

1280
01:28:43,399 --> 01:28:45,835
 Disengaging all locks.

1281
01:28:45,868 --> 01:28:46,969
I'm almost there.

1282
01:28:47,002 --> 01:28:48,905
Disengage.

1283
01:28:52,775 --> 01:28:53,876
( chimes )

1284
01:29:18,167 --> 01:29:20,503
It worked, guys.

1285
01:29:25,507 --> 01:29:27,643
( grunts )

1286
01:29:29,778 --> 01:29:31,647
Oh, no, Tory.

1287
01:29:37,052 --> 01:29:39,455
( heroic theme playing )

1288
01:29:40,989 --> 01:29:42,124
Deoxys.

1289
01:29:42,157 --> 01:29:43,626
( laughs )

1290
01:29:47,729 --> 01:29:48,831
Pika.

1291
01:29:50,732 --> 01:29:51,934
Pikachu.

1292
01:29:58,674 --> 01:29:59,776
Pika.

1293
01:30:02,845 --> 01:30:04,814
( chuckles )

1294
01:30:06,982 --> 01:30:09,585
Pika! Pika!

1295
01:30:11,220 --> 01:30:13,556
( chuckling )

1296
01:30:17,092 --> 01:30:19,662
Pika. Pika.
( laughs )

1297
01:30:19,695 --> 01:30:21,731
Pika!

1298
01:30:31,240 --> 01:30:33,543
( roars )

1299
01:30:41,049 --> 01:30:44,554
SNORLAX:
Snorlax.

1300
01:30:47,990 --> 01:30:49,959
( all chuckling )

1301
01:30:59,234 --> 01:31:01,070
Tory.
Daddy.

1302
01:31:01,103 --> 01:31:03,239
( Tory laughs )

1303
01:31:03,272 --> 01:31:05,608
Tory.
Hi, Dad.

1304
01:31:05,641 --> 01:31:08,043
I'm so happy
you're safe.

1305
01:31:08,076 --> 01:31:12,615
But I'm only okay
because of my friends.

1306
01:31:25,627 --> 01:31:27,897
TORY:
Come on, guys. That tickles.

1307
01:31:41,310 --> 01:31:42,878
PIKACHU:
Pika.

1308
01:31:42,911 --> 01:31:45,081
( majestic theme playing )

1309
01:31:53,055 --> 01:31:55,925
Goodbye. I'll miss you.

1310
01:32:00,796 --> 01:32:03,065
I wonder where
they're going.

1311
01:32:03,098 --> 01:32:04,767
Yeah.

1312
01:32:04,800 --> 01:32:08,170
But now, wherever they go,
they'll always have each other.

1313
01:32:08,203 --> 01:32:10,072
Pikachu.

1314
01:32:23,051 --> 01:32:24,152
Hey, Pikachu?

1315
01:32:24,186 --> 01:32:27,590
I'm glad that you and I
will always have each other.

1316
01:32:27,623 --> 01:32:30,759
Pika. Pikachu.

1317
01:32:30,792 --> 01:32:32,662
( Bree Sharp's
"This Side of Paradise" plays )

1318
01:32:35,297 --> 01:32:37,933
I must have lost
20 pounds so far.

1319
01:32:37,966 --> 01:32:39,702
And you already lost
your mind.

1320
01:32:39,735 --> 01:32:41,604
And I'm losing
my patience,

1321
01:32:41,637 --> 01:32:44,139
so just shut up
and keep pedaling!

1322
01:32:44,172 --> 01:32:45,908
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

1323
01:32:45,941 --> 01:32:50,680
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la
La, la, la, la, la ♪

1324
01:32:52,848 --> 01:32:54,850
 ♪ There's a place I know ♪

1325
01:32:54,883 --> 01:32:56,852
 ♪ It's always jumping ♪

1326
01:32:56,885 --> 01:33:00,990
 ♪ I'm thinking we should go
And leave our worries ♪

1327
01:33:01,023 --> 01:33:03,225
 ♪ You've got a friend in me ♪

1328
01:33:03,258 --> 01:33:05,194
 ♪ And I'll tell you something ♪

1329
01:33:05,227 --> 01:33:09,331
 ♪ This time
